{align:justify|Hanh Doan - Late 2016}
{align:justify|TEARS OF THE TREASURY}
{align:justify|This happened more than 20 years ago, at that time during the "Great Cultural Revolution" the country's situation was boiling over.}
{align:justify|That year, I had just accepted a job as a driver for the district's transportation company. At that time, the whole district had two opposing parties: "Bo Duoc" party and "Tsunami" party. Most of the company's employees belong to the "Song Than" side. As for me, I don't like to get involved in politics.}
{align:justify|It was just fall, because the city wanted to carry out three major projects, so our unit had to work quickly. The company ordered more than ten young drivers to form a team and go to a neighboring district more than two hundred kilometers away to transport construction materials. Only my car was responsible for carrying wood. Therefore, every day when the fleet departs, my fellow drivers and I only walk side by side for about half of the route, then go our separate ways. Everyone takes care of their own transportation.}
{align:justify|I drove straight along the route to the wood factory and when I returned to the city I was the lone runner on the route. From the district to the wood workshop, there are two roads: A paved road, running smoothly, delicious but long and far; a rough, winding dirt road but quickly reaching the destination. If I take a shortcut, I can save gas because it shortens an hour. Usually when I go, I always choose a shortcut, but when I'm busy coming back, I choose the asphalt road, because at this time the vehicle is heavy, and driving on bumpy roads will not be safe. Another worrying point is: Going on a country road, you have to pass a large cemetery, containing more than a thousand graves. When I set out in the morning and ran on this road, I was not afraid, but when I returned, it was dark and I had to go through the cemetery alone, so I didn't have the courage.}
{align:justify|But there were two times I ran back on this country road at night and it was completely unexpected that those two times suddenly saved my life!}
{align:justify|Lần thứ nhất: After loading the goods, it was already dark, of course I had to drive along the paved road. But as soon as I started the engine, I suddenly saw a big white rabbit appear in front of the car, making me curious and decided to chase it. At that time, the financial world knew: Rabbits like to take shortcuts, especially when there is light shining on them, as if they are hypnotized by car lights, they keep running and running until they are exhausted and die. That's why there's a rumor: “Stupid rabbits!”.}
{align:justify|I was accidentally "captivated" by this rabbit so I chased it for a very long distance. By this time it was dark, the rabbit was exhausted, it ran to a gravestone, stopped and collapsed there. Then I woke up and realized I had driven down a country road and was now in a cemetery. I couldn't stop my whole body from breaking out in a cold sweat, but I still managed to get out of the car. Because the rabbit's white silhouette was very close, enough to draw me closer to it. When I picked up the rabbit, I discovered it was dead. I also saw the words engraved on the tombstone: “Kieu Tu Van!” When this name caught my eye, I immediately thought: "Lying in this grave must be a certain lady!". In my heart I silently said: “Please accept my sincere condolences!”. Then I quickly climbed into the car, drove furiously, running like crazy, just hoping to get home quickly.}
{align:justify|It turns out that on the night I drove down that shortcut, besides the asphalt road I usually used to go back to every day, there was a sudden bridge collapse, as a result of which more than twenty cars, not detected in time, fell into a disaster: Cars crushed, people died! And the time when this disaster occurred was when I usually returned home and often crossed the bridge.}
{align:justify|That evening, after I returned home, my two parents who had just met me burst into tears. When I heard the news that the bridge had collapsed and many cars and people were in trouble, I was very frightened. I didn't expect to have a lucky escape just because I chased the rabbit. Therefore, I did not have the heart to eat that rabbit, so my father buried it, showing some gratitude for his saving grace.}
{align:justify|The second time is: After about half a month, my car arrived at the lumber camp and saw a party. The factory manager eagerly invited me to stay for the party. When I said goodbye, he even took a jar of good wine and gave it to me and said: “Bring it home for your father to drink!”.}
{align:justify|When I sat in the cockpit, I realized that because I was having a party, I was already two hours late. Moreover, the alcohol was gradually taking effect, even though I drank very little, but I was like a very drunk person. I didn't understand why or what the devil was doing. In fact, when I returned, I never wanted to run on this rough road, especially at night. It seems like at that moment I only had the thought: Must get there quickly.}
{align:justify|But after driving for a while, the car suddenly turned off. I tinkered and adjusted everything but the car wouldn't budge. I was so tired that I was dizzy, because at that time I hadn't been in the job for long so I didn't have much experience repairing machines. The place where the car stopped was a large cemetery, and it stopped right in the exact spot where I picked up the rabbit's body last time. The three words "Kieu Tu Van" engraved on the tombstone can be seen clearly!}
{align:justify|I looked around, the faint moonlight shining down on the cemetery looked even more scary. My heart beat fast because it felt like countless eyes were peeking at me. So I quickly climbed into the car, picked up the jar of wine, and gulped it down to stop shaking. Then I collapsed on the steering wheel and fell asleep.}
{align:justify|The next morning, when the sun rose high, shining its iridescent rays on my face, I woke up. Looking from afar, seeing the farmers harvesting rice, my spirit gradually stabilized. I started the car to test... Still couldn't find what was wrong, so I had to walk to the wood workshop, they immediately sent a mechanic to repair my car. But this talented worker could not find the problem. So we had to ask a tow truck to tow the car back to the wood workshop. Because I had to go through a long period of painstaking editing, I was forced to stay there temporarily. Another day passes.}
{align:justify|On the third day, I finally drove home, but the situation here surprised me even more. In the district, all important roads are guarded by the Liberation Army.}
{align:justify|Each convoy of police cars carrying banners, constantly shouting, ran past. When I returned to the company, I learned that a bloody battle had broken out between the two parties "Bo Duoc" and "Tsunami". As a result, more than two hundred people were injured, and my agency also had eighteen employees in distress.}
{align:justify|When I got home, my mother burst into tears and said:}
{align:justify|- God has eyes, if my car hadn't been damaged, maybe I would have been in trouble and lost my life by now!}
{align:justify|After that day, my company suspended, three major projects in the district could not proceed. Time passes like that.}
{align:justify|To this day, I have transformed from an innocent young man into a man over forty years old, with a peaceful wife and children.}
{align:justify|In the spring of 2003, my father fell seriously ill. In his dying moments, my mother suddenly revealed a truth that shocked and shocked me:}
{align:justify|- Son, I am not your biological mother.}
{align:justify|It turns out, she is not my father's main wife.}
{align:justify|More than 40 years ago, my biological father and mother lived in a neighboring district. A few days after giving birth to me, my mother became ill with postpartum illness and passed away. A year later, my father married a widow who is now my current mother. Then due to a transfer, my parents moved to this town.}
{align:justify|The reason my mother had to tell this secret is because according to the customs of my hometown, when my father passed away, he was only allowed to be buried in the same place as his first wife, that is, my biological mother.}
{align:justify|A week later, my father closed his eyes forever.}
{align:justify|Under the guidance of my uncle, our group took our father's coffin to our hometown cemetery. When we arrived, my uncle pointed to a grave and said:}
{align:justify|- That is your biological mother's grave!}
{align:justify|As soon as I looked at the three words "Kieu Tu Van" engraved on the grave, I was stunned and immediately collapsed... then burst into tears, crying like rain and wind.}
{align:justify|From then on, I took a vow to be vegetarian, keep the five precepts, do good deeds, and release animals... Diligently practice the Buddha's teachings, always try to create more fields of blessings to dedicate merit to your parents}
{align:justify|Bao Khang}
{align:justify|MIDDAY ACCIDENT}
{align:justify|I am a woman with the surname Tang, good karma at the University of Chinese Literature, currently married for three and a half years and have a son, but my mind always yearns to leave the home life. That's why every time I go to the temple, my husband is often dissatisfied, leading to arguments with each other, because my husband firmly says: "It's okay to stay at a monk's house, there's no need to leave the home life!". I disagree, so I often argue with him. My husband can't stand being upset, sometimes he gets so angry that he has to smash and throw things... or go out to drink to relax, so our family is often in discord and confusion.}
{align:justify|At the end of February last year, a very heartbreaking thing happened: That day my husband was away because he had to stay overnight at the hospital to take care of his father who had suffered a stroke. It's just me and my little son left at home. Who would have thought that in the middle of the night, suddenly a man wearing black clothes, masked, holding a machete, broke in. He rushed straight into my room, injured me on the head, and used force to rape me. Before leaving, he also robbed me of my money and belongings.}
{align:justify|When my husband returned, I told him the whole accident. He was furious, extremely shocked, quickly bandaged my wound, and then took me to the obstetrics hospital for a checkup because he was afraid I might be pregnant. This time I suffered a sudden and painful accident, and in my heart I kept praying to Bodhisattva for protection: “Please don't let any more storms arise in my family.”}
{align:justify|Half a year after the accident, I still have nightmares. Not only did I dream that a thug came to rape me, but even every time my husband wanted to be intimate, I was still haunted by the story of the thug's humiliation, so I always reacted in horror, even thinking that my husband was a thug who wanted to rape me. Therefore, I have a very distasteful attitude towards my husband's intimate behavior, and even towards men, I also develop a grudge.}
{align:justify|Not long after that, we moved back to our hometown, and the hauntings of the painful accident in the past gradually faded. Every day I began to sincerely chant sutras paying homage to the Buddha, over a long period of time.}
{align:justify|Perhaps my devotion touched all Buddhas and Bodhisattva, so last year I finally met my master Wisdom. He was very sympathetic about my accident in the past and wholeheartedly saved me.}
{align:justify|Master took me to the main hall to burn incense and invite the wronged bondholders to come forward so he could preside and help clear the wrongful convictions.}
{align:justify|At that time I was extremely sincere, earnestly repentance, and prayed. Unexpectedly, he felt an apparition of inspiration. Soon the first unjust person appeared: There was a child who hugged a believer in the temple, expressing that he wanted to find me. But the attitude showed extreme resentment. She said she was the little girl I aborted, which scared me to death.}
{align:justify|Afterwards, I reflected and reflected, suddenly remembering that at that time we had just gotten married. We discussed it together, afraid that if we got pregnant early, we wouldn't have enough money to take care of the child, so my husband chose to let me take birth control pills bought at a pharmacy. Who would have thought that after taking the medicine, we would end up having an abortion. Without knowing it, we had accidentally killed an unfortunate little life.}
{align:justify|Then this little girl also expressed: Because he wanted to avenge my malice, he often harassed my son and made him cry loudly, and even made him cry for a long time. No wonder the boy kept crying for no reason and cried so fiercely. Sometimes he seems stubborn and difficult to teach, only likes to play alone and often argues. Whenever I tell him not to play with dangerous things, he always does the opposite. Sometimes he even runs into the middle of the street on his own, even though his parents chase after him and shout at him, he doesn't even bother to turn back. Sometimes he even fiercely fought back against his mother.}
{align:justify|That's why sometimes I can't stand it, so I have to spank the boy. But since he had the good fortune to approach his master and listen to the Buddha's recitation, the boy became much gentler and appeared to be very obedient and easy to teach, this is a very strange phenomenon.}
{align:justify|The second suspect is a girl. She said that I was a man in my previous life.}
{align:justify|In that life, she originally intended not to get married and wanted to become a monk. But because I harbored the evil intention of possessing her, I took the opportunity to rape her, causing her to become pregnant and give birth to a child, causing her to embrace sadness and death.}
{align:justify|Because my wish to leave the home life was destroyed by me, she holds a huge hatred, always wanting to avenge me, so her consciousness is often around me, always creating all kinds of obstacles to disturb and prevent me from practicing! Even though my heart was focused on Phat, I never had the chance to approach Master or listen to any sutras or dharma. Furthermore, you have caused my marriage to fall into misery, deadlock, and no way to save yourself.}
{align:justify|After that, she took further revenge, controlling and luring a thug to break into my house to rape and rob me of my money and jewelry. Let me taste again the feeling of being raped that she had to endure in her past life. It caused me both body and mind to be tormented, in severe pain, so miserable that I didn't want to live.}
{align:justify|Now I understand that the reason I was raped, slashed, and injured in this life is related to the crimes I committed in the past. I am aware of each retribution that falls on my body. It is true that I have sown the wind so I must reap the storm. Whenever I commit a crime, I must receive retribution, there is no injustice at all.}
{align:justify|During the time the evil retribution came, my mind was very unstable, I constantly complained, silently blaming why all the Buddhas and Bodhisattva did not protect me? Why are the police so bad and not good at solving cases to catch the perpetrator who harmed me and punish him severely according to the law to match his crime?}
{align:justify|But now, after understanding the cause and effect, I immediately make vows before Buddha: From now on, I vow to make every effort to practice, completely stop evil and do good, strictly adhere to the precepts, practice according to Buddha's teachings, and vow to help people understand cause and effect and understand Buddha's teachings. For my husband and children, please take care and love with all my heart, never use anger to act.}
{align:justify|When I finished making vows, not long after, many wonderful things happened, beyond my imagination! The atmosphere in the family has changed, becoming warm and harmonious. My husband used to have a jealous personality, and he always doubted and didn't believe anything I did. I just had to chat with someone for a few words, and he was staring at me very uncomfortable, losing my freedom. Even in front of my brother, I didn't dare mention any other man's name. Otherwise, he will forever be suspicious of you.}
{align:justify|But now, things are different. No matter who I go with, what I do, what I say... he had absolutely no doubts. If I discuss Dharma with anyone, not only will he be very happy, but he will also listen attentively and seem very interested. He also did not restrict me from doing good, on the contrary, he encouraged and encouraged me. He never stopped me from going to see Master, so I was free to study the Dharma and listen to the sutras.}
{align:justify|Three or four years ago, my brother and I often argued non-stop. The atmosphere in the house was very gloomy, even the chickens and dogs were not at peace. But since I was determined to improve myself, swear to stop evil and cultivate good, to abandon bad and embrace good, within just a short month, my family was in harmony and enjoyed abundant happiness.}
{align:justify|“Wife and husband together can dry up the East Sea”, now my whole family is vegetarian, my children are very obedient and easy to teach, different from before. Even though he is a vegetarian, his health and condition are developing extremely well. Everyone complimented: My child is full of heaven, has a very good appearance and is a great man.}
{align:justify|Following Buddha's teachings, strictly maintaining precepts, stopping evil and doing good, life will be very happy, my family is an eloquent proof. Do you want to try the app? If you sow good causes, you will reap good results. If you want to not suffer, don't sow evil.}
{align:justify|Why did we have such a magical transformation like in the movie?}
{align:justify|I think the main reason is no more than three points:}
{align:justify|1.I sincerely repentance towards those I have harmed in the past, determined from now on, to correct mistakes, innovate, not create evil, not make mistakes again.}

