{align:justify|Recently, thanks to believing in Buddha's sincerity, he has obtained many wonderful things. Under the guidance and support of his master, his incurable disease has now healed.}
{align:justify|It turns out that this teacher in his previous life was a Great Mandarin of the Qing Dynasty, because he often used cruel and brutal torture on prisoners, especially fond of using whips and staffs... whipped the back of the victim, whom he beat to death so much that it was unspeakable. In addition, he often used humiliating punishments and even broke the prisoners' legs.}
{align:justify|Therefore, when the bondholder's unjust complaint appeared, his hands kept shaking, his legs also became disabled, unable to walk, his mouth was always moaning and screaming, constantly blaming the sky for injustice: “You are so cruel, why are you still a teacher in this life?”…}
{align:justify|Master has explained many times: The good and bad fate of each person depends on the cause and effect of retribution. We cannot draw conclusions from the manifestations of one life, because the hidden causes sown in many other lives also have a related influence, so we should not blame heaven and blame others, do not develop jealousy.}
{align:justify|But because in order to atone for past mistakes, it is necessary to express sincere repentance, so this teacher, right at the scene, knelt down towards the unjustly complaining bondholder earnestly repentance, expressing his utmost repentance. Furthermore, it also provides them with the following:}

