{align:justify|Female monk}
{align:justify|SAVE A MONKEY, A MONKEY SAVE A VILLAGE}
{align:justify|In the dense forest of Kim Buddha Son (Chongqing), there is a touching story between monkeys and humans as follows:}
{align:justify|At the end of July last year, in the northern mountains, mountaineer Vuong Chi Thanh went into the forest to pick medicine and met a blue-black furred monkey (more than two years old) whose left arm was injured. He immediately carried it home, took care of it and bandaged its wound, and let it rest at home.}
{align:justify|After a week, the monkey's wound healed, he left, but every day he still returned to visit Mr. Vuong, even helping with housework.}
{align:justify|Sometimes wild boars, porcupines and other animals come to steal food and fruits from the garden, this monkey often chases them away, scaring them away.}
{align:justify|One day at the end of September, around 3:00 a.m., Vuong Chi Thanh was still sleeping in his house when he suddenly heard a violent banging on the door and screaming that woke him up. He quickly opened the door to look and saw the monkey coming to visit. He went to hug it, but its attitude showed a strange panic, it dodged from his hand and cried out loudly.}
{align:justify|Mr. Vuong was bewildered and did not understand. The monkey pointed his hand behind the mountain. Vuong watched, he was horrified to see that on the mountain, the rocks were collapsing and large rocks were falling continuously. The monkey reached out and pulled Mr. Vuong away. Mr. Vuong finally understood: Danger was coming, so he rushed into the house, shook his wife and children, and they all ran out.}
{align:justify|Next he went knocking on each door. The whole village has 5 households, a total of more than ten people. They were able to run out and escape while the giant rocks were falling, destroying all the houses in the village. After escaping death, many villagers burst into tears and said:}
{align:justify|-It's so dangerous, if it weren't for this monkey to save us, we'd all die.}
{align:justify|After the villagers had escaped, they gathered together to look for the benefactor who saved their lives. They discovered the monkey on a tree, looking at them with love and joy, making a "squeak" sound from his mouth.}
{align:justify|After reading this story, please everyone please refrain from killing and releasing animals. Because giving life to things is also giving life to ourselves, saving people is also saving ourselves. The act of saving and releasing lives brings immense benefits and merits that are indescribable.}
{align:justify|A SESSION TO OBSERVE cause and effect}
{align:justify|Hearing the Sutra Translation Institute announce that Layman Qua Khanh and his daughter from Thien Tan were coming to preside over the Dharma conference and answer questions about cause and effect, I rushed to attend.}
{align:justify|This was the first time I saw layman Guo Khanh and his daughter Guolin.}
{align:justify|I asked myself, just over 20 years old, why does my heart often hurt? Moreover, I always have asthma, feel short of breath, have difficulty breathing... But the hospital couldn't find the cause. I knew I was sick, but I didn't understand the cause. At that time, I didn't think I was sick due to cause and effect.}
{align:justify|When they heard me ask the question, both father and son closed their eyes for about ten seconds, said nothing, then saw Qua Lam nod, then shake his head again.}
{align:justify|After opening her eyes, she told me: On her body are countless shrimp, fish, crabs, aquatic species, seafood... They were all competing to report the sins she had committed to them to me, so they couldn't let her live in peace.}
{align:justify|I immediately announced that I was a vegetarian.}
{align:justify|Qua Lam closed her eyes again, a moment later she opened her eyes and told me:}
{align:justify|- The sick beings above explained that: Even though she is a vegetarian, she enthusiastically teaches and guides people on how to cook salty dishes, such as how to prepare shrimp dishes.}
{align:justify|At this point, I was speechless and confused, because the answer was beyond my imagination.}
{align:justify|In my entire life, I have only taught someone how to cook shrimp once, and at that time no one witnessed it, so why does someone know so well? Could it be that those animal consciousnesses clearly understand every thought that arises in my mind?}
{align:justify|At that time I burst into tears, feeling like I was so wrong. As soon as I apologized to the animals I had eaten, I swore: Later, not only did I not eat, but I also advised people not to eat. At that time, I cried profusely, with tears and runny nose running, regardless of whether the hall was crowded with five or sixty people.}
{align:justify|Now Layman Qua Khanh spoke up, he said that what I did was sincere repentance. He advised me to start reciting Buddha to pray for Buddha deliverance for those miserable sentient beings. I had just recited a few Buddha's words, when Layman Qua Khanh said:}
{align:justify|- Amitabha Buddha has appeared above the center of the hall…(1)}
{align:justify|We raised our heads to look, at this moment I had an extremely strange feeling, like I had just lifted a big rock from my heart. I felt extremely refreshed and comfortable in my chest and was able to take a long, clear breath, feeling incredibly relieved. My heart is now pain free, no longer uncomfortable... It's really impossible to describe the state of happiness and joy at that time.}
{align:justify|At that moment I bowed to all Buddhas and Bodhisattva in the ten directions, thanking us for giving us the opportunity to be reborn. I also bowed to laypeople Qua Khanh and Qua Lam, thanking them for their explanations, helping me understand cause and effect and also showing me the method of eliminating karma. If on the path of studying Buddha, I have achieved any achievements, it is all thanks to the great merit of the two guides.}
{align:justify|Next, Layman Qua Khanh and his daughter were busy answering cause and effect and everyone's illnesses until the lecture ended.}
{align:justify|I went home that night and discovered that my legs, which previously couldn't be crossed, could now be cross-legged, and I could even sit all day. Hearing my whole body feel light, I feel like my practice of studying Buddha is going a long way compared to before.}
{align:justify|So I was very confident, thinking "I'm fine". But that night when I went to bed, I suddenly discovered something very strange: It seemed like there were many strange objects traveling on my body, and their moving targets were all pointing towards my heart and chest. This happened when I was not yet asleep, my mind was extremely alert.}
{align:justify|I quietly followed and discovered: First there are many things crawling from my elbow up to my biceps, at the same time there are many things crawling from my knees up to my thighs, there are many things crawling up from my belly, the things above my head are moving down.}
{align:justify|It means that behind me, in front of me, all over me, there are many moving objects, some moving fast, some moving slowly. But they all aim at the same goal: My heart and chest, it seems they decided to choose those two places as their base of refuge.}
{align:justify|This whole process took less than a minute, I didn't feel scared because I was reciting Buddha. Although I have partly guessed the situation, I still need to ask someone with wisdom to help me verify for sure.}
{align:justify|A few days later, I attended the cause and effect lecture conference by Qua Khanh and Qua Lam. The young girl (sitting next to me) also has the ability to trace cause and effect to help people. I asked her to look at it for me: Is there any aquatic species that has not followed all Buddhas and Bodhisattva but is still residing on my coals? This girl looked around for a while, then replied:}
{align:justify|- On coal you have many aquatic species, fish, shrimp, etc.}
{align:justify|I asked: How much is left?}
{align:justify|She said:}
{align:justify|- There are so many, too many to count. They are worn all over your body. Especially the two places where the heart and chest are filled...}
{align:justify|Afterwards, thanks to layperson Qua Khanh and his daughter's explanation, I clearly understood and realized the following:}
{align:justify|Because I have eaten too many animals for more than twenty years, especially aquatic animals. Therefore, my body is always in pain and suffers from many diseases. Even though these animals are dead, their resentment has not yet dissipated, so their consciousness comes to reside on my body. That's why my one word, one action, one gesture, one move... Everything is understood by them.}
{align:justify|They know that the heart is an important place for the organs and the chest is an important place for the organs, so they decided to base themselves there! They first choose to reside in the heart, followed by the chest, then the abdomen, head and limbs.}
{align:justify|Depending on the number of sentient beings I kill, eat... increased, but my heart and chest became more and more seriously ill. When they were upset, they gathered together to bite, sting, and tear my flesh to eat... to resolve hatred. This is when I felt an extreme pain in my heart and chest.}
{align:justify|After Amitabha Buddha appeared and took away the sentient beings on my body. Those who agree will go, those who don't will stay, continuing to direct me towards revenge and debt collection. Why is it that right now I think: “I'm fine now”, that idea is very misleading, because think about it: What kind of merit and virtue do I have, that I can rely on a few Buddha chants or just one repentance to eliminate all those great sins?}
{align:justify|These sentient beings who decided to stay and refused to leave, saw that my heart and chest were two perfect places to take revenge, so they decided not to leave, and even fought for space. That's why that night when I went to bed I discovered that there were many objects moving on my body. Perhaps during the day they also "march" to compete for my heart and chest, but because the day is busy and not as quiet as the night, I don't detect it.}
{align:justify|Since I had an "uninvited guest" come to the capital like this, since then I have been unable to meditate (how embarrassing), currently I can only meditate for about an hour.}
{align:justify|Having clearly understood the problem, it must be resolved. Because there are many sentient beings on my body who do not want to go, and repentance is a very effective method of resolving resentment, so I decided to practice repentance, ask for forgiveness from the wronged families, I repent and create blessings... Praying for them is also helping yourself.}
{align:justify|Right here I also recall a cause and effect story that Qua Khanh and Qua Lam find difficult to reconcile:}
{align:justify|There was a monk who practiced very diligently, but his heart was seriously hurt. Both father and son of the Duong family saw the reason: There is currently a big fish residing in his heart. Layman Qua Khanh and his daughter advised the fish, but it refused to leave.}
{align:justify|After Qua Lam talked with it for a while and then interpreted it, he realized that this fish was asking the monk: You must remember for yourself when, where, and for what reason did you kill him? If you remember and repentance, it will go away immediately. Otherwise, don't try… And there's no need to discuss or negotiate anymore, he also won't let Layman Qua Khanh and his daughter interfere and help.}
{align:justify|This poor monk thought for a long time but couldn't remember... So the other fish refused to go.}
{align:justify|I don't know if he has remembered yet?}
{align:justify|I tell this story because I want to say: The injustice has a head, the debt has an owner. After I finished repentance, Amitabha Buddha was only able to take away a part of the unjust bondholders, the remaining was more than half, they refused to go and decided to stay and take revenge right on me.}
{align:justify|I have absolutely no doubt that all Buddhas and Bodhisattva can help me eliminate karma, but they have already helped me a lot, the rest must be up to me to save myself and resolve the resentment until the creditor forgives me. I need to put in a lot of effort, if I do it then I can bear it... Isn't it always said in the sutras: Do we need to repentance a lot?}
{align:justify|The monk's story provided me with a good method of repentance, because the perpetrators always want us to remember how we wronged them, so I started to recall everything: Try to remember all the species, including chickens, fish, ducks... Under what circumstances did I eat and kill, which part, where, how much, and when? I try to remember everything meticulously, then chant Buddha's name or rebirth mantra for sentient beings to repentance.}
{align:justify|I cried and recited, because I discovered that I had killed and injured too many sentient beings, because I was afraid that I would miss sentient beings, so I had to find the Encyclopedia to look up more. As a result, I discovered that there were a number of sentient beings that I had eaten and forgotten about (because I hadn't eaten for a long time), because now I have become a vegetarian, so there are many sentient beings that I have forgotten. I then repentance, dedicating merit and discovered this method is extremely effective.}
{align:justify|When I just started repentance, remodeling… then discovered that there were many species moving around on the body, but this time was different from before, because their target was: Get out of my body. For example, from the knee they move down to the ankle, before reaching the foot they disappear and are no longer seen.}
{align:justify|After that, depending on the number of repentances I increased, the number of objects on my body gradually decreased. Later, I felt like there was almost nothing moving on my body anymore.}
{align:justify|I think, if it is possible to invite these sentient beings, it is also thanks to the power of all Buddhas, Bodhisattva and the blessing of the Buddha's name.}
{align:justify|Let me tell you another interesting thing: The Shurangama Sutra and Mantra are very powerful and can make people immediately abandon salty foods and become vegetarian, of which I am the clearest proof.}
{align:justify|Before going to the US to study, there were many times I wanted to become a vegetarian, but my mother didn't allow me to so I had to give in. After coming to America, I was too busy studying so I didn't think about becoming a vegetarian.}
{align:justify|One day, thanks to my friends to invite me to the City of Ten Thousand Buddhas to attend a Dharma conference, I had the opportunity to request a set of the Shurangama Sutra to bring home. At that time, I did not know what the Shurangama Sutra preached, I only heard my friends say: "In this sutra there is a very good mantra, especially for people living alone in America like me, it will provide very good protection..."}
{align:justify|So after returning home, I started reading the Shurangama Sutra. After reading a few pages, I didn't understand anything so I quickly turned to the mantra and started reading each word, trying to concentrate my mind and meditate there. This is the first time I read the Shurangama Mantra, of course it is not easy to read, because there are many words I have never seen before, just depending on each mantra, symbol... but try to read every word.}
{align:justify|So the miracle happened: Not even halfway through reading the note, I suddenly decided to become a vegetarian, and was even more confident that this time I could do it. As soon as the idea of vegetarianism arose, faith also arose, so solid that even I was surprised. I immediately ran out of the room, opened the refrigerator, checked all the food I had, and removed all the salty foods. The innkeeper heard the noise and immediately ran over to ask. After knowing what she said:}
{align:justify|- Why don't you wait until you finish eating all the canned salty foods before becoming a vegetarian? It would be a shame to throw them away like that!...}
{align:justify|Her words and posture were full of resentment, it seemed like she thought I was too stupid. I must know that if I throw away food, it means wasting a lot of money. Because just counting the reserved chicken thighs, it's enough for a week because I spent a lot of money on stored food. But at that time I only knew that I no longer wanted to eat these things, so I was determined to eliminate them. When I heard the landlady say she could use it, I gave it all to her, making her jump with joy.}
{align:justify|A week later, I got sick and had such a fever that I couldn't get out of bed. The landlady cooked porridge for me to eat, including some minced meat.}
{align:justify|I'm very upset, but I can't eat without eating. Results: I just ate a mouthful and had to crawl to the bathroom and vomit it all up. I understood Bodhisattva's intention, so since then for more than ten years, I have never eaten salty food again. Moreover, I don't crave anything, and at the same time, I also abstain from eating five new foods.}
{align:justify|Thanks to all Buddhas and Bodhisattva's great compassion, I hardly wasted any effort in giving up salty food.}
{align:justify|I figured it out: You should not give people salty food, nor should you buy salty food for them. Now I know the sin I have committed, so I earnestly repentance. I think the salty food I wanted to throw away should not have been given to anyone.}
{align:justify|After I had good karma, I went to Cuu Kim Son (2) for work. Before looking for a house to rent, I silently prayed to all Buddhas and Bodhisattva to arrange for me to find a place to work near home, with a comfortable room to rent, security, and a landlord who knows how to be vegetarian.}
{align:justify|My biggest concern was renting a room, because I didn't like all the places I looked at, so I finally chose a place.}
{align:justify|When I looked at the house and decided to rent it, I had to go to the landlord's store to deliver the money. At this point I was stunned, because the owner's restaurant was a vegetarian restaurant. Only later did I realize: What I pray for is not unsatisfactory. I was so grateful, I sincerely bowed to all Buddhas, Bodhisattva.}
{align:justify|There is a female student living in the same house as me. The other day when I was preparing to cook, she was also working in the kitchen. While waiting, I saw that she wanted to make shrimp but was clumsy and didn't know how to prepare it.}
{align:justify|Before becoming a vegetarian, I was the king of eating seafood, so shrimp, fish, crab... I am a gourmet and a great cook. From a young age I was always taught: When eating seafood, you must choose the type that is still alive to be sweet, delicious, and nutritious.}
{align:justify|Looks like she's clumsy and doesn't know how to make shrimp. Even though I was a vegetarian, my mind was not yet pure, because I was "bloody heroic and came out to help". I went up to the teacher and showed her in detail how to make, how to cook, and how to prepare the shrimp to make it delicious and enjoyable.}
{align:justify|By now I know I was wrong, so here I sincerely apologize. Actually, I shouldn't have been teaching people how to make salty dishes, so I was blamed by the shrimp spirit and took revenge.}
{align:justify|After summarizing, I have drawn eight important things:}

{align:justify|I use a new analytical method that is not flawed, this method is for stupid people (because I am inherently stupid).}
{align:justify|For example, about fish, I have eaten plaice, eels, carp, tilapia, shark, goldfish... Then I try to remember clearly the number of pomfret... How much carp have I eaten and where? How much carp have I eaten and where? Just like that, reminisce and repentance. Next is buffalo meat, how much have I eaten and where? My experience is that you absolutely should not miss any sentient beings, so when you clearly remember the list and number of species of sentient beings harmed, you will understand how many times you need to repentance to be pure.}
{align:justify|I have repentance a lot. When I succeed, I can sleep peacefully at night and sleep very well.}
{align:justify|This is my personal experience, I sincerely share it, I hope you all benefit.}
{align:justify|Ly Thap Phuong}
{align:justify|DO NOT EAT FISH}
{align:justify|I am a woman in Zhejiang, Taizhou, 46 years old this year. For the past ten years, I have suffered endlessly, like living in hell on earth. I know that bad karma is blooming, it is the injustice of the bondholder's doing.}
{align:justify|Two years ago, seeing that I could not bear all the suffering, my aunt took me to take refuge in the Three Jewels, whose dharma name is Phap Dao. After that, I continuously organized three great delivery ceremonies for unjust bondholders inside and outside the body to pray for them to be reborn, to leave suffering and be happy.}
{align:justify|Since then, all other sufferings have disappeared, only the pain in the body has not decreased, but has increased in severity. Sometimes I feel pain like I've been bitten by an insect. Sometimes the pain feels like being stung by a scorpion, and the painful areas are red and very uncomfortable. Ten days ago, my face had painful red pimples, so painful that I didn't want to live, so I knelt in front of the Amitabha Buddha statue in my house, tears pouring down like rain, I cried to Buddha:}
{align:justify|- Dear Amitabha Buddha, in the end do you exist or not? Have you seen that my face is full of red pimples and is so painful that I don't want to live?}
{align:justify|Just like that, I cried and talked for several hours.}
{align:justify|The next night, by chance I learned that Master Trinh Ba Duc had come to Shanghai to lecture, instructing how to "eliminate karma", I knew this was Amitabha Buddha's instructions, and thought to myself: “I am saved.” So my mother and I immediately went to Shanghai to attend his lecture. It was July 7, 2013, I had the good fortune to meet Master Trinh Ba Duc and clearly understand the principle of "all sentient beings are one".}
{align:justify|During the Dharma conference, other practitioners all benefited, there was a clear feeling, but only for me the red spots on my face became even more fierce, I knew that this was an unjust being who did not agree to be saved!}
{align:justify|Among the students, there is Ms. Xuan who has attained the Divine Eye, she told me:}
{align:justify|- I saw on her body a big black fish that was very spiritual, with long horns on its head.}
{align:justify|This fish cried and told Ms. Xuan: In my past life, I ate its meat and chewed its head too (so I received revenge from it, making my brain dull and not wise). The fish's anger and hatred made it impossible for the fish to reincarnate into the human world. On the one hand, it followed me to take revenge to torture and punish me, causing me to suffer enough pain. At times, it tortured me so much that I did not want to live.}
{align:justify|The fish also said that it was doing it lightly, because it saw that my mother had stopped being a vegetarian and reciting Buddha for more than twenty years, so it "relented" and did not take revenge on me. Because this fish loves Buddha's Dharma very much, it gets extremely angry every time it sees me going to the "evil sect" for help because of the unbearable pain. At those times, it tries its best to push me back to the Buddha sect. Even though this fish witnessed countless, boundless sentient beings and countless of its relatives, thanks to Master Trinh's transcendent teachings, they were led to the Pure Land, but it absolutely refused to be reborn.}
{align:justify|Miss Xuan immediately asked the fish what kind of conditions she wanted to give me? Then it says: Even though I sincerely repentance, it is still not enough and requires me to do two things:}

{align:justify|I have a stupid nature, so as soon as I heard that, I immediately thought: “I can do the first request, but the second, in this coastal activity, where can I go to advise 100 people not to eat fish?...}
{align:justify|Master Trinh immediately advised me to write an article online (doing so not only advises hundreds, but also thousands of people, even thousands of thousands of people not to eat fish!)…}
{align:justify|I immediately repentance, making vows: Please meet the two conditions of the required fish.}
{align:justify|Master Trinh showed compassion because I continued to perform the delivery ceremony for that fish. Even though its descendants and relatives were all reborn, it still said: Right now it doesn't want to be reborn, but in the future it won't torture me anymore, but it wants to continue monitoring me for a while, see how I study, if I sincerely correct my mistakes, and if my behavior is consistent? Then, it will suddenly leave without warning.}
{align:justify|Thank you Amitabha Buddha, thank you Master Trinh, thank you to the generous and generous fish who compassionately forgave me and pushed me on the path of diligently studying Buddha.}
{align:justify|After the Dharma assembly, my illness has subsided, but I am still accepting my sins, so even though I have to endure this little suffering, I am willing to repay it. Because I think: Compared to the pain when the fish I killed and ate, my pain is only one thousandth of the pain it had to endure in its past life.}
{align:justify|Let's take a look, the aquatic species are swimming freely, traveling freely in the water, but the world has spread nets, hooked hooks, exploded explosives and used all kinds of methods to catch them: Skinning, scaling, disembowelment, decapitation, and internal organs make them bleed profusely and are extremely painful. I brutally kill them to prepare delicious dishes, even roast them alive right when they are struggling, I torture them to the extreme. Don't they embrace this hatred to the core?}
{align:justify|Let's see that today, humans raise aquatic animals, let them live in dirty, polluted water, and use food mixed with chemicals to stimulate growth. When we eat them, not to mention the parasitic worms, interest... all move to reside in the human body, causing people to suffer from all sorts of illnesses and suffer torment from the evil karma of killing.}
{align:justify|Think about the feelings of hatred and pain that animals suffer and sympathize with them.}
{align:justify|At this moment, I use my own painful experience, while shedding tears, to write these lines. We implore and advise you to stop eating fish from now on, including other animals such as: Buffalo, cow, pig, goat, chicken, duck, bird, etc. You should also not eat, which means don't eat salty food anymore.}
{align:justify|Buddha taught: Living beings are inherently identical, and were once related to each other's children and parents. And because all sentient beings do not want to be killed, eaten, or harmed, "don't do to others what you don't want to do!"...}
{align:justify|May all people and animals live in harmony, love, and happiness. May this earth always be green and fresh. May the surrounding environment always be carefully preserved by people, making the scenery always perfect with beautiful blue water and mountains. May all sentient beings live happily and cultivate successfully.}
{align:justify|Because I have had the experience of being tortured like hell on earth for more than ten years by unjust people, I sincerely advise you: Please don't eat fish, because right now you still have a lot of blessings so you don't see any retribution, but once the evil results come, it will be very difficult to endure, difficult to live and no one can bear that pain for you. This is the painful lesson I have learned in this life.}
{align:justify|Phap Dao}
{align:justify|SCREENING EVIL REPORT}
{align:justify|This morning, someone in Vietnam brought two children to see me, saying their health was not good, hoping I would help them have everything go smoothly as expected.}
{align:justify|These two children were mentally abnormal. As soon as I saw them, I immediately recognized them, so I asked them if they had ever killed anyone? After their mother listened to my explanation for a while, she understood and told:}
{align:justify|There used to be a giant tree. They cut it down and saw two snakes under the tree, they had crawled into the cave.}
{align:justify|At that time, these two children used boiling water to pour into the cave to kill the two snakes.}
{align:justify|After doing that, their eldest son locked himself in his room. A few days later, when he came out, he developed a mental illness. The first son is like that, the second son is like that, both have mental illness, the mother hopes I can help them resolve this.}
{align:justify|This disease is related to killing. Because they act cruelly and without compassion. The two snakes had already crawled into the cave, but they still poured boiling water that killed them. These two snakes were originally two brothers. When they burned them to death, they themselves went crazy.}
{align:justify|karma for killing living beings receives very severe retribution. Just kill and be told: Mutual killing, mutual retribution, this is a very tragic thing in the world, even though people do not understand or believe that creating karma will result in evil retribution, but revenge and debt retribution constantly happen, creating national wars, causing karma to kill each other! The deeper the karma, the more serious the crime, so keep killing.}
{align:justify|In 1980, a Director from far away Southeast Asia came to the City of Ten Thousand Buddhas to ask me for help, because he had a very serious case of cancer. I will take you to the main hall and make repentance announcements before all Buddhas, Bodhisattva and the four assemblies in the ten directions to save your karma.}
{align:justify|He said he had committed many crimes and had eaten countless living beings' meat such as monkey brains, goose feet, etc.}
{align:justify|Then I asked:}
{align:justify|- Have you ever killed someone?}
{align:justify|He said: Absolutely not! But I told my wife to get pregnant!}
{align:justify|I explain:}
{align:justify|- So, he developed a terrifying incurable disease because all these lives came to him, demanding his debt!}
{align:justify|I would like to remind you: You should not have an abortion and should never persuade someone to have an abortion, because doing so is the same as murder!}
{align:justify|The person maintaining the precepts has the merit of maintaining the precepts; Those who break the precepts will receive evil retribution for breaking the precepts. Speaking of cause and effect, whether you have received precepts and observed the precepts or not, cause and effect always exist and operate! The act of killing (killing the fetus) is very wrong. According to the law of cause and effect, you must definitely suffer retribution.}
{align:justify|All of this killing only increases resentment, invites strange and evil diseases into the body, accompanied by unusual symptoms that are difficult to explain and incurable!}
{align:justify|Now, besides cancer, there are other incurable diseases. These diseases first originate from committing adultery, killing, stealing, lying, using intoxicants, and injecting drugs...}
{align:justify|When everyone keeps the five precepts, practices the ten virtues and fasts, there will be no natural disasters and will enjoy many great blessings. Even a pure mind will cause many people to have supernatural powers and open the five eyes.}
{align:justify|The stories of sick retribution are real, they are the teachings of the Dharma, but people in the world do not believe them. Most of them still try their best to create evil, not knowing how to stop killing or releasing animals... If we want world peace, then everyone should keep the five precepts: Don't kill, don't steal, don't commit adultery, don't lie, don't drink alcohol or take drugs... If you don't create bad karma, the world will have no natural disasters, suffering, or illness, and people will live happily.}
{align:justify|Venerable Master Hsuan Hua}
{align:justify|WHY YOU SHOULD NOT MURDER}
{align:justify|You remember the old story in history, the day King Ty Luu Ly killed all the Shakyamuni Buddha family, the Buddha's head also suffered from painful pain. What is the cause? That was in the distant past, when the Thich family was a fishing village and the Buddha Shakyamuni Buddha was a boy in that fishing village. When the fishermen caught a big fish and were about to kill it and eat it, the Buddha's predecessor playfully hit it on the head with a stick three times. That big fish was the predecessor of King Luu Ly. When he was born as a human, he killed all the Shakyamuni Buddha family, and the Buddha also had a headache in return.}
{align:justify|You can't help but believe this! The retribution is very clear and terrifying. For this reason, Buddha strictly prohibited killing.}
{align:justify|Not only does Buddha have compassion for humans, but he also has compassion for tiny ants. Because in the Buddha's view, all living beings can become Buddhas. In the Pham Vong Sutra, it says: "All men are fathers, all women are mothers." Sentient beings circulate in the six paths, each being each other's parents and relatives. Therefore, killing sentient beings is also considered killing one's parents.}
{align:justify|People do not know or believe this theory, so they freely kill and devour each other. You need to deeply believe in cause and effect. If you deeply believe in cause and effect, then even if your heart has not changed, good deeds will still be achieved, because every time you act and think, you always know how to carefully consider, so your behavior will naturally follow the good direction.}
{align:justify|Those who often have accidents are caused by evil karma, especially emotional karma. You must know that disasters happen because you have sowed evil in the past. Therefore, the accidents of war, floods, fires, and earthquakes are all caused by the ripe fruit of karma, which has come to fruition, so you must accept it.}
{align:justify|Good deeds result in good deeds! The proof is that in the last two World Wars, only overseas Chinese in Australia were safe. Why? Because in their past lives they never created karma!}
{align:justify|In the year of the Tiger (1914), I was preaching the sutras at Long Hoa Mountain, when 4 districts in Dali prefecture had a terrible earthquake, Dali was the heaviest: The houses and citadels all collapsed and nothing remained. Only the temples and stupas are okay, still standing as before. During the earthquake, the earth shook and cracked severely, and a fierce fire spread throughout the area. People scrambled to escape, then the ground suddenly cracked under their feet, causing them to fall down and get stuck in it. They tried their best to climb up, but as soon as they emerged, the land closed in, cutting off their heads and leaving them stranded on the ground. The horrifying scene looked like a living person being trapped in a hell of cutting or burning, so miserable that the eyes could not bear to look.}
{align:justify|Several thousand households in the city died, and very few survived. There are two gold shops here: Van Xuong shop of the Trieu family and Tram Nhien shop of the Duong family - when the fire reached the homes of these two families, they immediately extinguished themselves. The place where they live has not been affected by earthquakes. Each of these households only has a few dozen people, but all are safe. The reason is that these two families, who have lived forever and always give blessings, are able to receive such rare good results. Anyone who knows about them is moved.}
{align:justify|If you are a Buddhist, you must understand this cause and effect that is difficult to fathom and believe deeply without doubt. If you deeply believe in cause and effect, you will voluntarily do good, maintain the precepts, live long and no longer dare to kill.}
{align:justify|Venerable Hu Van}
{align:justify|FISH}
{align:justify|I was born in 1982. Since I was little, I have been very interested in Buddha's teachings. When I was in my teens, I started to come into contact with Buddhism. When I read the Six Patriarchs Sutra, I found it easy to understand, and I really liked the sutra text.}
{align:justify|But karma itself is still deep and heavy, so I have not really practiced, because even if I read books and sutras, I only understand the superficial surface.}
{align:justify|Until 2009, I had the good fortune to meet Master Tinh Khong to listen to the teachings of the Infinite Life Sutra... and the big door to a new life path... suddenly opened before my eyes.}
{align:justify|At that time I practiced reciting the Buddha's name, but my mind was not strong enough, my recitation was not continuous and often interrupted, and my mind's progress did not increase. It wasn't until after experiencing retribution that I truly changed on my spiritual path.}
{align:justify|In the winter of 2009, I followed my uncle to Shenzhen to stay temporarily. He loves fishing. One afternoon he fished in the lake and caught a fish weighing 8kg and brought it home. I happily killed it (really embarrassed because I was so stupid).}
{align:justify|When I hit its head 7 or 8 times in a row, it struggled very hard. At that moment, anger arose in my heart and I wanted to punish it to relieve my anger, so I put down my knife.}
{align:justify|Three days later, that night I was sleeping, dreaming, when suddenly I felt like there was a pair of huge hands, constantly punching, pounding, pinching, interrupting me... even used its monstrous (extremely heavy) body to press on me. I was very scared inside but didn't know what to do. I quickly recited Namo Amitabha Buddha continuously. I kept chanting, not daring to think of anything else. About ten minutes passed, then I saw a white light appear outside the window (in front of me), this light was not dazzling, warm, making people feel comfortable, the heart became calm and from the Buddha's face appeared, indescribably solemn, in front of the Buddha also appeared a pond, inside there were many lotus flowers, extremely beautiful, at that moment all the fear in my heart disappeared.}
{align:justify|After going through this experience, I clearly understand that cause and effect are real. If it weren't for Buddha and Bodhisattva's help, I would have been in big trouble, so I bravely repentance the act of killing, chanting sutras dedicating merit for the sentient beings I killed.}
{align:justify|Through this experience, I believe that Buddha and Bodhisattva are always with us, always ready to help. As long as we single-mindedly practice and recite His name constantly, the response will arise and we will be protected by their powerful blessings.}
{align:justify|Since then I have developed strong faith in Buddha's teachings.}
{align:justify|Ly Nam}
