{align:justify|Yin Yang EYES}
{align:justify|My grandmother told me that when she was young, when she had free time on the farm, she made incense (as a side job). She did not add any chemicals to the incense, to show respect, because this was an offering.}
{align:justify|Perhaps thanks to making incense with a pure heart, when she was over 30 years old, she was seriously ill and was saved by Bodhisattva (on the street she met an old Buddhist monk who helped her heal).}
{align:justify|This old woman prepared medicine to treat my grandmother. After taking the medicine, my grandmother recovered, but since then her spiritual eyes have also opened. Regardless of whether it is day or night, she can see another dimension that our physical eyes cannot see.}
{align:justify|In the past, I completely did not believe in the theory of heavenly eyes or yin and yang eyes because she always saw species that I could not see, so I always told her: She has a mental illness! And consider her old-fashioned, feudal, superstitious...}
{align:justify|Later, since I had the good fortune to listen to Buddha's teachings and then develop the intention to enter the Dharma, I understood and appreciated what her yin and yang eyes saw, because this helped increase my faith a lot.}
{align:justify|I would like to tell you the reason why I practice following Buddha.}
{align:justify|A few years ago, I was walking on the street and met an eel seller. Seeing them peeling the bones and skinning the eel, I felt so impatient... So I decided to buy all the live eels in pots and take them to a pond in a nearby park to release them.}
{align:justify|Since I was a child, I've been afraid of snakes, so I'm afraid of animals that have the same shape as us. That's why I didn't dare catch the eels in the bag, so I had to ask my sister and I to take them to the park and ask her to catch them and release them into the pond for me. Because I was so scared, I just stood far behind and looked. Results: When the eels were released into the water, many of them swam closer to me, they looked healthy, and more than half of them poked their heads above the water, gathered around me, kept nodding and bowing in gratitude. I clearly realized what they meant, the funny thing is, they didn't gather around my sister even though she was very close to them, but instead swam to surround me and kept bowing, it took a long time for them to leave.}
{align:justify|Witnessing this strange scene, at that moment I was extremely surprised and touched, so moved that tears streamed down my face and I understood what it meant: All sentient beings are equal, animals and people inherently have the same spirituality!}
{align:justify|In the past, I was a salty food lover and always opposed vegetarianism. Whenever a meal comes and there is no meat or fish, I refuse to hold chopsticks. But after releasing the eels and returning home, my mind changed. I was no longer interested in eating salty food. I began to study the Buddhist scriptures to understand more about the miracles in life and silently thanked the eels for helping me enter the Buddha gate.}
{align:justify|At first, I read the Ksitigarbha sutra, then every month on the ten days of the month (the 1st, 8th, 14th, 15th, 18th, 23rd, 24th, 28th, 29th and 30th) I chant the Ksitigarbha sutras.}
{align:justify|My grandmother was illiterate and didn't understand anything about these ten days of boyhood, but every time it was ten days of boyhood, after I got home from work, she always asked me: Are you going to chant the Ksitigarbha sutras today?}
{align:justify|I asked in surprise:}
{align:justify|- Why do you know?}
{align:justify|She replied:}
{align:justify|- How could I not know! She saw that the demon realm beings had already gathered in the house since the afternoon, so many that she could no longer count them! They came to hear you chanting sutras!}
{align:justify|There were days when it was too dark and I was still working, and she came up and said:}
{align:justify|- Don't do it anymore, worry about chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras! Don't let those sentient beings kneel and wait for a long time, it's very sinful and not good!}
{align:justify|Moreover, she also clearly described the scene: The demons only gather on ten days, which are the days I choose to chant the sutras. She saw that among them there were both animals and people, the dead were wearing clothes belonging to their dynasty.}
{align:justify|I used to love salty foods and didn't like being vegetarian, so I made her suffer because of me, she had to kill many evil karma creatures.}
{align:justify|During the time I was chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras, those sentient beings who were killed and eaten all came to listen to the sutra, there were enough pigs, shrimps, chickens, crabs, fish, etc.}
{align:justify|Especially one time the crabs came, waving their big claws, as if she wanted to say that my whole family used to eat crabs, they listened to the chanting sutras with great joy.}
{align:justify|Now I no longer chant the Ksitigarbha sutras, but my main practice is the Diamond Sutra, the Heart Sutra, the Shurangama Mantra, etc. Of course, there are always sentient beings from other realms gathering to listen.}
{align:justify|Learning Buddhism is about letting go of attachments, but there are still many people who practice more and more attachments. Attachment to the bondholder's unjust body, afraid of the bondholder's unjust body causing trouble to him, so he wants to give up and not practice.}
{align:justify|Mr. An Quang once said: Don't you know that ghosts and humans are always mixed together? Because there is no place without ghosts! Even though we don't invite ghosts, every house has ghosts. It is estimated that the demons present are hundreds of thousands of times more numerous than humans. If people are afraid of ghosts, they need to accumulate virtue and do good deeds. Surely the ghosts will respect them and protect them.}
{align:justify|If people do things secretly, the demons will compete to insult them, so it is difficult to live in peace.}
{align:justify|If you know this clearly, then even if you are alone in a dark house, you should not have any bad thoughts or evil thoughts, let alone do wrong things...}
{align:justify|If demons are good demons, they will make way when they see people coming, and when people leave, they will occupy the entire land.}
{align:justify|If Le Devil (evil devil) appears, it will be a great omen.}
{align:justify|You must know that there are always many people (good or evil) in front of everyone. If you want to not be afraid of ghosts, you should: Keep a good mind, speak good words, do good deeds, then the demons present will become your guardians.}
{align:justify|Just afraid that: There aren't many demons that I respect. If they have more, the better, so what's the point in being afraid?}
{align:justify|Now I would like to talk about the sound transmission of sutras. Thanks to luck, I learned about this merit. If possible, you should arrange a place to pronounce (promote the sutras) in your architecture. If so, the surrounding environment will be radically transformed and have enough capacity to guide people's minds. Like the Pure Land of Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara's Putuo Mountain...}
{align:justify|The huge benefits obtained are: Right in the area where the mantra is pronounced, not only people, but also insects, all sentient beings there are exempt from falling into the three evil realms, and can be reborn in the heavens, humans, or the Pure Land of all Buddhas.}
{align:justify|Because the evening is very busy, I changed it to: Every day chanting sutras early in the morning. In my house, I bought two machines for regular menstruation: A DVD machine that specializes in playing scriptures, notes… I placed it at Buddha street, a generator of "Manjushri Mind Mantra" I placed on the table in the study room. I hope I can help sentient beings who come to listen to the sutra to benefit at all times.}
{align:justify|When I opened the DVD and played the sutra disc, I attracted many predestined beings to listen, among them was a dragon. The first time my grandmother saw its giant figure, she screamed in horror: Oh my! This snake is so huge!}
{align:justify|She also described it as located outside the terrace of the Buddha altar. It also hovered back and forth in the yard, keeping watch. I advise you not to be afraid but look carefully: That giant "snake" you described, does it have claws or not? She looked closely and answered yes. I explain: That's not a snake, but a Dragon (the Dragon God who protects the Dharma!).}
{align:justify|This year that dragon appeared again, this time it was in the air, where the Manjushri Heart Mantra came from.}
{align:justify|In Buddhist scriptures, it is often mentioned that the Eight-fold Thien Long, the Dharma-protecting Dragon Thien, etc. But everyone doesn't understand this idea.}
{align:justify|Buddha Shakyamuni Buddha, before entering nirvana, advised the Dragon King and the Gods... Remind them to uphold Buddha Dharma. Because it has been over two thousand years old, many people still think this is an unrealistic myth, impossible to believe.}
{align:justify|I am truly grateful to the wise men and women who have guided me on the path of practice and practice, also grateful to her yin and yang eyes, grateful to Long Thien protecting the Dharma for showing up... makes me have enough faith in Buddha's teachings.}
{align:justify|The story I told is completely true, if you don't believe it, just consider it as if you heard a myth. And I firmly believe that: This world really does exist species that humans cannot see through.}
{align:justify|If you raise your head three meters away, there are gods, so we must observe and review every thought that arises in our minds at every moment.}
{align:justify|May dedicating this merit to all sentient beings in space throughout the dharma realm, may all practice together and attain enlightenment.}
