{align:justify|BURTY SUTRAS TO SAVE THE MOTHER}
{align:justify|The entire Qua Tru lay family belongs to the intellectual class, all three generations are university professors.}
{align:justify|Layman Guo Tru, right when his mother was seriously ill, sincerely devoted himself to worshiping the sutra dedicating merit for her mother. This filial piety touched heaven and earth and that diligence caused the mother to be preserved from the demon gate.}
{align:justify|Please listen to her recount what she went through:}
{align:justify|My parents, before retiring, used to teach the subject "Plant protection and insect control" at a university in Triet Giang. My mother was originally a multi-literate female scholar, who contributed many great scientific research achievements, contributed to profound teaching, it can be said that she had many students all over the world, she was awarded the title of "Distinguished Professor" and received government subsidies.}
{align:justify|Currently, my parents are over 70 years old, even though they have been retired for many years. But because they have achieved extraordinary achievements in the field of insect control, they are always invited to work at the Agrochemical Factory. I am not familiar with my parents' killing habits, because even at home, the two of them still research and prepare "Insecticide" medicine to supply to the Agrochemical company, earning a lot of money thanks to this preparation profession.}
{align:justify|Ever since I was a child, I have witnessed my father having nightmares every night, always screaming in terror that someone wants to kill him, moreover, his skin is not good, rough and prone to sores like scabies. On his bedside, he often keeps a bottle of plaster all year round.}
{align:justify|When my father taught at university, he often suffered from a mysterious illness, this pain constantly tormented him, and later he also suffered from coronary artery disease, often suffering from tuberculosis and fear, making him unable to take medicine from his mouth, his face was always sad, and he could not smile.}
{align:justify|Thanks to a good fate, I happened to read the book "Retribution for the Present Life" by layperson Qua Khanh, and clearly understood that my father's illness was related to his work. Also understand that: Because we created bad karma and ate meat and seafood every day, we suffered evil consequences.}
{align:justify|So I started chanting Ksitigarbha sutras for the animals my parents and I killed and ate, hoping to deliverance to them, asking for their forgiveness.}
{align:justify|At first there were no obvious results, but every day I still tried chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras... Not long after, one day my mother said:}
{align:justify|- My three children have been sleeping very peacefully recently, they no longer have nightmares, and their constipation has also improved. His face was also much better, he looked cheerful and cheerful, and he even stopped smoking.}
{align:justify|I was extremely happy and silently thanked the mighty merits of the Ksitigarbha Sutra. The result is unimaginable.}
{align:justify|After that, I was fortunate to read "cause and effect Supplement to Luong Hoang Sam" by Qua Khanh. The true stories in the book made me much more frightened and shocked. I secretly knew that my parents had committed a very serious crime of killing. I needed to immediately stop eating salty foods, repentance of killing karma, enter the path of studying Buddha, and practice immediately.}
{align:justify|Even though my parents' bodies are getting weaker and weaker, they haven't awakened yet and are still creating constant karma, so what should I do?}
{align:justify|Thinking of my parents who went through so many hardships to raise me, I have been studying Buddhist vegetarianism for several years. Now I really want to replace my parents and repentance with the sentient beings who were killed by them. In the sutra "Buddha's theory of karma reports differences" it is said: If any living being worships a Buddha stupa or temple, they will receive ten merits:}
{align:justify|Get a good reputation for beauty}
{align:justify|If there is a statement, everyone will believe it}
{align:justify|Be fearless, not afraid of others}
{align:justify|Favored by God}
{align:justify|With full authority}
{align:justify|Beings like to come close}
{align:justify|Often close to all Buddhas, Bodhisattva}
{align:justify|There are enough great blessings}
{align:justify|Death to eternal life}
{align:justify|Quickly attaining Nirvana.}
{align:justify|The Buddha Sutra is a dharma treasure, representing the Buddha's wisdom, the dharma body of the Buddha's relics, so the merit of worshiping the sutra and worshiping all Buddhas is not different, just like the merit of worshiping the Buddha stupa, the ancient virtue has its taste through worshiping the Avatamsaka Sutra, the Lotus Sutra, etc. but enlightenment. So I decided to worship every word in the "Ksitigarbha Sutra" for my parents, with a strong heart and sincere devotion, I would be able to feel Bodhisattva's blessings, bring benefits to sentient beings who have been harmed, and eliminate karma for my parents.}
{align:justify|While worshiping the sutra, I was secretly afraid that my merit was not enough, so at the same time I also worshiped the Lotus Sutra of the Wonderful Dharma, following the "one word, one bow" method. I worship one page of each sutra (about five hundred prayers). In addition, every day I take advantage of the opportunity to recite a book of the Shurangama Sutra. During this time, although my body is very tired, my mind feels very comforted and full of joy.}
{align:justify|When I finished worshiping the four chapters of the "Ksitigarbha Sutra", my mother accidentally fell and broke her left leg, and had to be hospitalized to have her artificial bone replaced.}
{align:justify|I suddenly remembered that in the past, when my mother lectured in class, because she wanted the students to understand better, she often used pins to pin insects' heads, or pin their feet to the board as teaching aids to supplement the lecture. Oh my! If you don't know the Buddha's teachings, it's easy to commit sins. If you move your mind and recite nothing, you won't create evil. Such causes must be like that. The cause and effect retribution is not wrong at all. Currently, the repentance flowers have bloomed on your body. If it weren't for me making vows to worship and repentance on your behalf, causing the heavy sins to be lightened, then the evil consequences you will have to receive in the evil path in the future will be miserable and unbearable to look at.}
{align:justify|When I finished worshiping chapter 7, my mother fell again, this time the injury to the back of her head, as a result of the CT scan there was bleeding, the skin was swollen, the hospital announced that her condition was critical, my mother appeared in hell, looked scared, couldn't open her eyes.}
{align:justify|At the same time, at home, my daughter and I, who was teaching at the university, couldn't open our eyes and felt equally miserable. This could be a deep emotional connection, or it could be that my child and I are helping the mother pay karma at the same time. My sister wanted to help her mother open her eyes, so she used a black cloth to block the light for her. The whole family was very tense.}
{align:justify|I ask everyone to stop killing, my brother making vows: Please fast for three months for my mother.}
{align:justify|The afternoon my mother was admitted to the hospital, that night we spent about 2,300 USD and went together to release her. At the same time, in the process of worshiping the sutras, I also try to recite two more sets of "Ksitigarbha", which means reciting four sets of "Ksitigarbha" every day, worshiping one page of the Ksitigarbha Sutra, one page of the Dharma Flower. I firmly believe that my sincerity can move the sentient beings who collect debts from their mothers and Buddhas and Bodhisattvas will bless them.}
{align:justify|The second day, after the release, I called my younger brother and asked about my mother's condition. He said:}
{align:justify|- Still the same, neither good nor bad, the doctor is watching.}
{align:justify|I feel like the bondholder doesn't want to leave her, because resentment is indigestion! Right then I decided to spend 1,650 USD to release animals and the next day to release 600 kg of snails. I knelt before the Buddha to repent on behalf of my mother, my mother's deep love, thinking about the difficult consequences of nurturing her, I shed tears, pleading with the Buddhas and Bodhisattvas to be merciful to save my mother, to save her unjust bondholders... Pray for my mother to have a chance to correct her mistakes and renew herself. If my mother leaves, what should my family do? Please Buddha Bodhisattva compassion, the wronged bondholders are generous in forgiveness.}
{align:justify|A few days later, my mother's illness gradually changed from good to good. This made the doctor feel strange and surprised. The sin of death can be avoided, but the sin of living is hard to forgive! My mother had to endure painful training, and her suffering also appeared on my body. Whenever she vomited at the hospital, at the same time I vomited at home, vomiting like crazy... to the point where you can't even drink water. At that time, my mind was very strong, I held the brass close to my side, and thought to myself: Even if I die, I must die before Buddha. I am willing to pay for my mother's life. If so, then great! Thanks to that thought, I persevered in worshiping the Ksitigarbha Sutra to completion.}
{align:justify|Layman Qua Khanh said: There are some unjust bondholders who will forgive you, but before they leave, they may bite or tear you... Harassing your body, this is the principle of repaying a heavy reward with a light reward. So all night long, for several hours, my mother's whole body convulsed, suffering from pain... The doctor had to stay on duty all night to treat him, but later when he had a health check, the results were normal.}
{align:justify|The next morning, while I was chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras for my mother, there was a black shadow above my head. It wasn't until I started to worship the Ksitigarbha sutra that the shadow disappeared. I know that the unjust bondholders who resided on my mother's head are gone, and I also understand that my mother no longer has any residual effects. The doctor once said: An elderly person like my mother, who is already sick and has suffered such a serious brain injury from a fall, really has no hope of being saved. If she survives, she will have serious after-effects that will be impossible to handle on her own.}
{align:justify|I know that the profession my parents work in commits killing, a serious sin, so I decided to worship a set of Ksitigarbha sutras for my parents, and at the same time worship every word in the Vien Giac, Shurangama and Phap Hoa sutras, continuing...}
{align:justify|Every day I bow one thousand and one hundred times, and also try to recite four sets of Ksitigarbha Sutras, a book of Shurangama, Vajra and Bao Khiep An Sutra, Shurangama Mantra, Four Elements of Purity and Repentance.}
{align:justify|I really risked my life, my parents' injustices appeared on my body, plus my own karma debt was already deep, so my body was extremely unstable, but I secretly understood that if we owe a debt, we have to pay it, this is natural, let alone the debt we owe is limitless and limitless. Currently, the sentient beings who are being killed and eaten do not want to claim the fate of my parents, they just want their bodies to suffer. If it weren't for Buddha's blessing, I wouldn't be able to do it thoroughly.}
{align:justify|Because in the past, we did not tire of creating evil, so today we have to endure hardship and suffering to redeem ourselves. Thanks to that thought, I diligently chant sutras, pay homage to the Buddha, I believe in what the Buddha preached, His words to me are the truth, so I increase my steadfast faith.}
{align:justify|Currently, my mother is soon healthy and discharged from the hospital. Not long ago, when she returned to the hospital for a check-up, the famous neurologist also said: A person with a head injury who is over seventy years old like my mother has such a lot of bleeding but does not have to undergo any surgery. The swelling and accumulated blood and bruising can dissolve on their own and function smoothly without leaving any sequelae. It must be said that since the hospital's founding, this is the only incident he has witnessed for the first time! We must call this a strange thing in the human world!}
{align:justify|It seems that falling, getting sick... My mother was in danger, my parents suffered from many illnesses but were healed. My mother was resurrected and returned from the dead, making it difficult for my relatives and friends to believe. No one dared to believe that after falling and sustaining such a serious injury, she could still live and live very well, because she was not tormented by any after-effects.}
{align:justify|Do you believe it? Right now my mother is going online to look at stocks (I'm not suggesting playing stocks, I just want to tell this story to prove my mother's health level), proving that all her thoughts and judgments are still very sharp and agile.}
{align:justify|She herself said that most of her relatives came to visit her. Before that, everyone thought that she must have misaligned eyes, crooked mouth, foaming mouth, and half of her body unable to move. But when they saw that she was healthy as if nothing had happened, everyone was surprised, everyone almost praised her for being strange!}
{align:justify|My mother thanks to this, she became a famous figure, because it was widely discussed at her university assignment, when everyone heard that she asked her daughter (me) to worship sutras, chant sutras, pay homage to the Buddha... Describing the merit of saving her, many people were deeply moved and grateful. They also develop the mind to recite and worship the Ksitigarbha Sutra. Even my father began to respectfully copy the Ksitigarbha Sutra with his pen.}
{align:justify|I hope that those who read this article, even if their body is currently in good health, should: Quickly give up eating salty food, for the sake of the things you have killed and eaten... Only by reciting Buddha or worshiping sutras, dedicating merit to them can we hope to avoid the moment of disaster, at which point even if we regret it, it will be too late.}
{align:justify|If I have any merit in writing this article, please give that merit dedicating merit to your parents. I pray that my parents will soon develop great repentance, study Buddha, and become vegetarian. May the two of you live long and be healthy and prosperous.}
{align:justify|Mr. An Quang once said:}
{align:justify|Forms of religious practice such as: Praying, chanting, chanting… are all dominated by respect. Even if you are in the position of an ordinary person, if your sincerity reaches the extreme, you will attract inconceivable merit and gain great benefits.}
{align:justify|Justify: Parents have a deep gratitude that is difficult to repay. As a child, when your parents are seriously ill and on the verge of death... Please chant sutras for your parents, chant sutras, release animals... Helping your parents turn danger into peace, not only will you gain blessings and increase wisdom, but you will also be able to save your parents, this is true filial piety.}
{align:justify|THIEN DIEN GUARDS}
{align:justify|Heaven has angels, earth has gods and demons. Gods, heavenly generals... In heaven and earth, there are people in charge of investigation, called "Gods of Tu Qua" who specialize in supervising public works and crimes in the human world.}
{align:justify|In the Buddhist scriptures: Angels and demons both have five powers, these five powers are their blessings. They just don't have full access to gonorrhea, but the heavenly eye, the heavenly ear, the other mind, the destiny, the spirit... they all have enough. If compared, the power of an earth god is not equal to that of an angel, and the power of an angel is inferior to a person who practices spiritual attainment. But for us worldly people, their abilities are already very complete. Because every thought that arises in our minds, they know it all and write it down clearly... Wait until I die and then make a judgment based on that.}
{align:justify|When we start thinking, we also create evil, but when we commit actions, it is even more serious. If you understand clearly, then every time you start your mind or think... We need to always be careful for fear of retribution.}
{align:justify|If you have evil thoughts and do evil things, you cannot avoid evil consequences in the future. That's why it says: The net of the sky is vast, although it is sparse, it is difficult to penetrate.}
{align:justify|This true morality, few people know nowadays. If you meet people who have no good roots or blessings, and you tell them these things, they will laugh at you and say you are too superstitious and stupid... so it's all nonsense! Because they can't believe it, they can't accept it. But when the retribution appears, it will be too late to repent, and sometimes they do not know that this is the ripening of evil retribution.}
{align:justify|Because they do not believe, that is: Nghi! -The concepts: Greed, anger, ignorance, arrogance, doubt… All belong to the group of extremely great afflictions, hindering wisdom and causing you to commit limitless sins.}
{align:justify|In the Avatamsaka Sutra, Buddha preached: When every person is born, there are two gods always by his side, one named Dong Sinh, the other named Dong Danh, who will never leave you for the rest of your life. These two gods are on our shoulders, we cannot see or know, no one can see them. But these two Heavenly Men (also considered angels), do not leave you day or night. In the Buddha scriptures, they are also called by another name: Good and Evil children. One person considers good deeds all your life, one person considers evil deeds all your life. So think about it, what do you do without anyone knowing? Even if you do evil and no one sees it, do you think you can escape? No one can escape, it must be said that there is no way to escape, so those who collide and kill people in the dead of night and speed up to run away, eventually fall into the net of the law. If they escape, then this must be considered in addition to the unjust cause and effect in many lives between them and the victim, because there is nothing unjust or accidental.}
{align:justify|The two pupils, Good and Evil, are the two gods Dong Sinh and Dong Nam mentioned in the Avatamsaka Sutra.}
{align:justify|Buddha preached that: Throughout each of us's lives, there are two "Good and Evil Children" who follow us day and night, never leaving for a moment. If you often think that these two pupils are always with you, then why aren't you careful every time you start thinking, speaking, or creating? The Buddha's words were definitely not false, so he certainly did not deceive us.}
{align:justify|In the past, we had many opportunities to practice and study, were taught by our parents, teachers, and good friends, so we should do less evil and do more good.}
{align:justify|But now, people today often criticize the old traditional educational culture as antiquated, they don't need it, don't believe it, and their parents can't teach it, or don't have time to teach it... Professors also don't pay attention to this, so all our lives we only know how to indulge in afflictions, develop evil habits, and create countless sins. So how can we avoid falling and not be punished by "Heaven and Earth"?}
{align:justify|In addition to the two gods Dong Sinh and Dong Danh, there are also "Heaven and Earth ghosts and gods monitoring" the world, also recording the good and evil of people. These ghosts and gods are countless in number, all religions mention them and have records.}
{align:justify|Thus, every time we start our mind, think, speak, create... Can anyone hide it? Therefore, we need to overcome our afflictions and bad habits, correct our mistakes, innovate, and strive to be good. We must live towards sublimation, our goal is: Personality, behavior... must always be worthy, excellent, optimal, good. If so, of course we will be in a state commensurate with our conduct.}
{align:justify|Monk Quang Hoa}
{align:justify|I SAW TWO GODS BORN WITH THE SAME NAME}
{align:justify|Just now discussing the two gods Dong Sinh and Dong Danh, thanks to a special fate, I also saw them, their physiques were like 7-8 year old children (no wonder Buddha called them pupils).}
{align:justify|It was in the year of the Republic of Korea 56 (1967) at that time I was a Head Professor, teaching at Tu Minh Tu Buddhist Academy. School opens on January 14. But one day before that, the 13th, I had an outbreak of hemorrhoids, causing endless pain. What's even more worrying is because tomorrow morning is the opening ceremony.}
{align:justify|Buddha Tu Minh Academy held a very solemn opening ceremony, attended by many monks, members of Parliament and government officials. I must introduce everyone to meet and preach.}
{align:justify|But I'm so sick, how can I attend the ceremony? Well, I'll take the medicine and hopefully tomorrow I'll be able to stand and speak. So I went looking for plasters. I didn't expect to take the wrong medicine, so as soon as I applied it, the pain was excruciating, and I couldn't even stand up, blood and pus were flowing out. Oh my! The pain tormented me for half a day, I had to grit my teeth and try to go back to my room to sleep, but I couldn't sleep all night.}
{align:justify|The next morning, when I woke up, I immediately saw a pile of blood, pus, and mucus lying wet on the bed. Feeling very uncomfortable, I still tried to go to the ceremony. During the ceremony, I could only say a few sentences before sitting down.}
{align:justify|At noon, after eating, rest. I took off my robe, looked at the bottom of my robe, and saw a wet pile. How embarrassing and rude I was. Those who know I'm sick can sympathize, but how will those who don't know judge me? I had surgery and took medicine, but it still didn't heal. This time I have to ask Buddha for treatment. So I told my disciples:}
{align:justify|After the evening session is over tonight, all of you can leave. I want to stay in the main hall to worship Buddha, it's like risking my life with this karma hemorrhoid! If I make it through, then tomorrow morning I will continue the morning ceremony, but if I don't make it through, then tomorrow you will go to the main hall to carry my body down!}
{align:justify|After the evening recitation, I was alone in the main hall to worship. I address all Buddhas, Bodhisattva:}
{align:justify|- Pray to all Buddhas and Bodhisattva to bless my illness, otherwise I will have no way to continue my teaching duties. If my illness doesn't heal, I will definitely not leave. If I have to die, I will die here!}
{align:justify|After making up my mind, I still bowed. After praying until after ten o'clock, I wanted to go into a coma, but I still tried to stay awake and pray. By 10:30, I could no longer stand, because the day before I couldn't sleep, and the next day I was in pain all day, so I could no longer hold on and fell to the ground.}
{align:justify|After that, my body stopped moving, only my mouth could move. I whispered: We should go to Hai Trieu Avalokitesvara, there is a partition there, so even if we fall down, we won't get hurt!}
{align:justify|So I crawled to Avalokitesvara Hai Trieu, in front of Bodhisattva Avalokiteshvara chanting: “Namo, great compassion, great compassion, saving suffering, saving Avalokiteshvara Bodhisattva!”… I chanted until my mouth stopped moving. At this point, I had to bet with fate. I could no longer recite the words but still had the heart to deal with them. I focused all my strength towards Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara to pray:}
{align:justify|Dear Bodhisattva, please respond to me and make my hemorrhoids heal, otherwise today I... die here for Him to see.}
{align:justify|While praying silently like that, I suddenly felt dizzy, as if a wind was blowing, followed by a sound. I raised my head to look and saw a statue of Bodhisattva Avalokiteshvara sitting on the table, with two deities kneeling, their heads about the height of the Bodhisattva's knees. These two people are the gods Dong Sinh and Dong Danh. They reported something and Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara was preaching. I looked at them intently, thinking to myself: “It turns out that Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara called these two to present a report about me!”.}
{align:justify|No matter what they say, in my heart I have secretly calculated in advance, I believe that if I have a lot of good and a little evil, then my illness will definitely be cured. Because of thinking like that, my heart became excited. I turned around and saw that the two gods had disappeared. I then turned to Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara, asking permission to return to my room.}
{align:justify|I touched my hemorrhoid to check and saw that it was really gone, it seemed like my disease was completely healed.}
{align:justify|Whoa whoa! At that time, my heart was very happy, extremely grateful to Buddha and Bodhisattva for his kindness, this feeling is indescribable, because I got rid of that devilish hemorrhoid.}
{align:justify|This is something I personally experienced and witnessed…}
{align:justify|What I'm telling you is that I hope everyone knows and believes that every moment in each of our bodies there is a god monitoring and recording all our good and evil, so in the future each person will experience suffering and happiness depending on the good and evil karma they have created, this is not wrong at all.}
{align:justify|So you must follow the Buddha's teachings, practice according to the dharma, be very careful to preserve the precepts you have received, always be on guard, be careful not to make mistakes. Must write in the sentence: Even if you die, you must not violate the precepts. Because the precepts are the teacher, the precepts are also the Buddha dharma.}
{align:justify|Excerpt from “Quang Hoa Lawyer Promoting Ancient Dharma”}
{align:justify|ON THE HEAD OF THE THREE TRULES THERE ARE SPIRITS}
{align:justify|The Chinese have a saying: "Three meters above my head there is a god." There is another theory: "If you raise your head three meters to see the blue sky, you can lie to people, but you cannot lie to the sky!". This verse reminds us that in every moment we must control our thoughts, every action and thought, must be directed towards ending evil and doing good. As for the Buddha, it preaches: Each person has two gods on their body, the god Dong Danh and the god Dong Sinh. Divine Name is white, male, and specializes in good deeds. The god Dong Sinh is black, female, and specializes in recording evil. Whatever good or evil thoughts we have, the gods record them all. Therefore, it is best for us not to have careless thoughts and avoid sowing evil causes. If you accidentally create evil, you must return quickly and do not continue to violate the precepts. The Infinite Life Sutra says: God knows, sin is not forgiven.}
{align:justify|You must know that the gods specialize in recording the good and evil we create. Every month, more than six times they go to heaven and hell to hand over the book of good and evil. We, depending on the good and evil karma we have created, experience suffering and happiness. I tell these things to remind everyone to maintain the precepts seriously. Before studying Buddhism, I once read a secular magazine. Now I would like to tell the story published in it for everyone to hear:}
{align:justify|At the end of the Qing Dynasty, there was a scholar who wanted to go to Beijing to take the Poinsettia exam. This department opened in the spring, which meant the exam had to take place until the end of the year. Many people in remote areas rush to the capital right from the winter, hoping to attend the spring exam in time. In the Mainland, every time winter comes, the North is covered with ice and snow, whitening the entire region. Makes it difficult to see the path. If you set out and encounter snow covering the road, you will only have to wait, because there is no place to go.}
{align:justify|Student X encountered that situation on the way to the capital, so he was unable to continue his journey. Had to take temporary refuge in a popular inn. But the innkeeper was a young widow whose husband had just died not long ago. Scholar X thought to himself: "I'll stay here for one night, then continue on my way tomorrow morning"... Unexpectedly, the snow continued to fall, covering the road thickly, leaving him unable to depart, forcing him to continue staying at the inn.}
{align:justify|One day, then another day passes. The guest is a handsome young man, the owner is a beautiful, young widow, both of them are single readers, but they see each other every day, so their hearts are distracted...}
{align:justify|So the scholar went to the front of the lady's room. First, he raised his hand to knock on the door, then suddenly thought: “Don't! I want to take the Poinsettia exam. If I enter, I will commit adultery. Heaven will remove my name, I have to go back!”…}
{align:justify|As soon as he returned, the female owner also had thoughts of wanting to go find him. As soon as she walked out the door, she suddenly thought: “Tch! Very undesirable! I am a widow, it is only right that I must maintain chastity, why do I immediately forget all manners when I see a handsome man? Don't be like that, let's go back quickly!”.}
{align:justify|The scholar returned, unable to stop the rising fire of desire, and went to the front of the widow's room. When this guy knocked on the door, as soon as the widow opened the door, he quickly left, because he felt he shouldn't do that. Fear of committing adultery again... will lose reputation.}
{align:justify|In ancient times we had a theory: No matter how well you study, no matter how destined you are to pass the Poinsettia, if you commit adultery or create evil... Then the Heavenly Court will erase that Poinsettia title immediately. So when he arrived and she was about to open the door, he quickly returned.}
{align:justify|But the widow's feelings were overflowing, so she went to his room and knocked on the door... At this moment, her inner self spoke again, scolding her: Shouldn't be rude, so she returned.}
{align:justify|Just like that, they kept going back and forth... It's been a while like that. For the last time, the scholar stood up and opened the door. The two of them stood there, half forward and half backward, both willing and unwilling, undecided.}
{align:justify|Even before they fall asleep, they keep wondering if half of them want to commit a crime, half of them don't... Then suddenly I heard a sound in the air: You two jerking idiots, do you really want to make a mistake or not? We have written down and erased our retributions in the book of good and evil until it's all broken!}
{align:justify|After the sound finished speaking, something was thrown down. At this time, the two of them were sitting on the bed. As soon as they heard the voice, they were scared and trembled. They quickly picked up the object to see: It turns out it's a "Book of Records of Crimes", with their names clearly written on it:}
{align:justify|“XX is set to be the Poinsettia this year, and adultery will be disqualified. YY is a virtuous widow who will ascend to heaven when she dies, but now commits adultery... Next are rows of words that are continuously crossed out and filled in as follows: “Violence”, “no offense”, “violation” (then cross out) then write “no offense”, “violation”, “no offense”… Throughout the notebook, I kept writing back and forth like that and then completely erased it. Just looking at it made me feel confused, so the gods also got angry and shouted loudly.}
{align:justify|These two people just watched it and quickly left to their room. From then on, no one dared to have lustful thoughts or commit any more mistakes.}
{align:justify|The elders of the past, every time they told their children this story, they always affirmed: "Fornication will result in the loss of reputation, blessings, fortune, and power... is real". Therefore, in ancient times, children of the scholarly lineage were told this story to warn them and maintain their dignity like precious gems.}
{align:justify|If you have a good education, your morality and virtue must also be high, without shortcomings... just got a reputation. Considering that a secular person is still like that, he is already leaving the home life, we need to pay more attention to this point. Because once you commit sexual precepts: Blessings, longevity, merit... Everything will be destroyed, so monks must be very careful!}
{align:justify|Excerpt translated from "Thien Dam Precepts"}
{align:justify|EARTH SPIRIT}
{align:justify|The land is revered as "the righteous god of blessings", this name is combined with four words, and is not easily acquired or arbitrarily revered. Most ignorant people still mistake the Earth Earth for the God of Wealth, but that's not really the case.}
{align:justify|To be an Earth God, one must meet four things:}

{align:justify|In the tenth Ksitigarbha Sutra, it is mentioned and confirmed: If someone is vegetarian and practices well... Then the Earth God is very happy, always protecting the happiness and peace of that land.}
{align:justify|You should not think that once you have taken refuge, you will become a person of right mind, have blessings and good virtues, higher and far beyond everything. Please remember this sentence: “The way of high dragons and tigers is respected, virtue is respected by ghosts and gods!”.}
{align:justify|You must have enough good virtues for the demons to admire you. If virtue is lacking, the devil will despise you. Even if ghosts and gods are of the lowest rank, they still have five powers, while we don't have any. What we need is virtue and humility. If we practice with an arrogant mind and contempt for ghosts, gods or any sentient beings, then we are not worthy of being a true student of Buddha.}
{align:justify|Master Thanh Nghiem once told the story:}
{align:justify|When he and his disciples were at Phap Co Son, while walking on the road, they passed by a local Earth temple. He then entered the absolution. The disciple saw this and was extremely upset and said immediately:}
{align:justify|- Master, these are all part of King Yama's faction, so don't get involved... As someone who studies Buddha, how can he make offerings to ghosts and gods?}
{align:justify|Mr. Thanh Nghiem replied:}
{align:justify|- People who study Buddha need to have a humble mind towards all sentient beings. I pay my respects because Mr. Earth is also a virtuous and noble person, protecting the direction.}
{align:justify|After speaking, the two continued walking, but what happened next was very strange: When they passed through a field, the disciple was not careful and fell down, his lower body was covered with mud, and he sank deeper and deeper, unable to escape. Thanh Nghiem immediately understood and smiled and told his disciples:}
{align:justify|- Please quickly turn to Mr. Earth Repentance and say: As a Great Minister, you should not accept the mistakes of small people.}
{align:justify|If the disciple does as told, his feet can immediately step up.}
{align:justify|This story is true, you must know that being a Earth Land is not an easy thing, at least when you were young, you created a lot of good blessings and high virtues, benefiting a whole world of humanity. So after death, based on good fortune and deep virtue... Only one can become an Earth God. Therefore, you should not underestimate the merits of the Earth God, the God of the Earth also protects the dharma.}
{align:justify|Suppose you go to a certain locality, in this locality: People are in charge of people's things, ghosts and gods are in charge of ghosts and gods. And in charge of these ghosts and gods, some are Divine Emperors, Earth Emperors... Think about it, if the beings of the demon world had no one to control them, wouldn't they cause chaos? In the temple, there is worship of Gia Lam Bodhisattva, who worships every day. This person also manages the management of ghosts and spirits and protects the security of the monasteries.}
{align:justify|As a student of Buddhism, we need to be humble and polite towards everyone. Another direction is towards the Blessed and Virtuous God? Regarding this point, you must remember carefully, do not think: Once I take refuge, I look down on everything.}
{align:justify|Having taken refuge, if you see Mr. Tho Dia, you should still say goodbye, to show gratitude to him for protecting the locality and making the weather favorable. We should be grateful and learn from the good example of Tho Dia, because he did good deeds for the people of the entire region.}
{align:justify|Behaving humbly and politely like that is the only way to add more blessings to yourself. This point is very important and should not be forgotten.}
{align:justify|Rely on the Three Jewels: As a guide, relying on the Three Jewels, and being respectful towards Earth, is to thank him. You must know that absolution is absolutely not a substitute for taking refuge, it is not taking refuge in him.}
{align:justify|In life we must know how to be respectful and grateful, this is the necessary virtue and personality of humans, we should not be arrogant or arrogant, because high tribute and arrogance is a big taboo for those who study Buddhism.}
{align:justify|Each Buddha has a symbolic title such as: Buddha is All Dignified Virtues, Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara is Compassion, Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva is Filial piety, Mr. Manjushri is Wisdom, Gia Lam God is Loyalty, and Earth Earth is the main god of blessings because he has both blessings and virtue.}
{align:justify|We say goodbye to Earth, not to beg for anything, but just want to do like him, learn the act of serving, want to show our gratitude and appreciation to him.}
{align:justify|Therefore, everyone must practice skillfully and take care to protect the Dharma and the Ashram. When you practice the Ksitigarbha Sutra, you should respectfully thank the God Emperor and Earth Earth, that is to show gratitude.}
{align:justify|Monk Quang Hoa}
{align:justify|SEISMIC PROBLEMS}
{align:justify|All my life I deeply believe in two things:}

{align:justify|I want to say: Nothing happened without reason. Let's take the story of my husband and daughter, the fate is very bad. Even though I have studied Buddhism for many years, it is still difficult to let go and cut off.}
{align:justify|In a recent dream, I dreamed that in one life I was a poor baccalaureate, already married, but because I wanted to marry a younger wife, I abandoned my older wife. My current daughter was a young woman in her previous life and was raped by me. She said angrily: I hate you forever, I vow to destroy everything for you...}
{align:justify|When I woke up, I thought carefully and saw that it was right. In this life, I took on the body of a woman, took care of the house for my husband, then broke up. Currently my husband and daughter are as cold as strangers to me, they only contact me when they need money, other than that, they don't pay any attention to me.}
{align:justify|The things that happened to me are all real. Today, I only hope that those who have the predestined opportunity to read this article will be alert, single-minded and single-minded in their practice, follow the Buddha's teachings, choose a method of practice that suits their base, and practice thoroughly for liberation from suffering. Personally, I practice the Buddha recitation method.}
{align:justify|My parents passed away before I learned about Buddha Dharma. At the company, my parents were always praised by everyone as gentle, honest, and kind.}
{align:justify|But my mother died of esophageal cancer when she was 57 years old, and my father, when he was 63 years old, suffered a leg fracture that led to paralysis and passed away. My parents died within the same year, just three months apart.}
{align:justify|After my parents passed away, it left me with a lot of criticism. It almost made me feel worse than dying. There was a time when I really wanted to die with them.}
{align:justify|In such a mentally depressed situation, I accidentally learned about Buddha's teachings (truly grateful). At that time, my brother advised me to chant the Ksitigarbha Sutra. I practiced with one mind and one mind, without any distractions when chanting the sutra.}
{align:justify|Praying to Quang Muc to save her mother, I was moved by her great vow, so tears flowed profusely... At the same time, my heart feels like a knife when I think of my parents. It hurts so much that I don't want to live. Then I dreamed that Bodhisattva Avalokiteshvara told me:}
{align:justify|- Don't be too sad, your parents fell ill and passed away due to the influence of karma...}
{align:justify|Suddenly I understood: Because my parents killed too much. My mother likes to kill chickens, and my father likes to catch fish and shoot birds. In the Ksitigarbha Sutra, all the general conditions and karma of people, including my parents, are described. When I didn't know Buddha's teachings, I personally witnessed it. At that time, I thought that maybe because I was sick and lying in bed for a long time, being injected with drugs all the time, I had hallucinations. But that's not actually the case. Later, when I recited the Ksitigarbha Sutra, I saw a scene of unjust bondholders pretending to be relatives of the deceased, to lure them away... Then suddenly my mind woke up and I understood. Even the things I remember as a child are as clear as watching a movie on a silver screen.}
{align:justify|chanting sutras Ksitigarbha On the third day, I dreamed again that Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara said:}
{align:justify|- Your father has gone to the West, but your mother is still present: The upper body is human while the lower body has one leg like a goat, one leg like a cow...}
{align:justify|Originally, my mother, when she was alive in this world, loved to eat beef and goat, and often killed chickens. She had an esophageal tumor and had to be operated on. Just like how she killed a chicken, the surgery was like that, the neck was slit 10cm, the abdomen was also cut open... It's so pathetic that I can't bear to look at it.}
{align:justify|When he was alive, my father liked to catch birds and tie their feet. One day, he fell from a height to the ground, a distance of only about one meter, but broke his leg, leading to cerebral palsy and suffering beyond words. The reason why I tell you this at length is because I want you to understand clearly: Whoever hears the Buddha's teachings has great blessings, should wholeheartedly believe, pray, practice... and be grateful, know your mistakes, repent, and sincerely meditate.}
{align:justify|One more thing, before the night Wen Xuyen had a major earthquake, I had a dream and it was very scary:}
{align:justify|An angry Heavenly Man said:}
{align:justify|- You guys, the crimes of murder, religion, lust, and delusion, are not evil at all. Even those who study Buddha but don't agree with their mind or mouth, you must be allowed to taste your own evil results!}
{align:justify|After saying that, a celestial man shot out, trampled many people to death, and kicked down many houses. His feet were huge, intending to step forward and trample me. I panicked, quickly held the white iron armor to cover the top of my head, continuously chanted Namo Amitabha Buddha and escaped. Woke up, sweating profusely, and heard the dog across the street barking very loudly. I immediately sat up and read the sentence: "All possessing appearances are false"... to reassure myself.}
{align:justify|And then at noon the next day there was an earthquake in Wen Xuyen.}
{align:justify|The third thing is, when I was studying Buddhism, there was a time when I often ran around. As for practice and practice, reciting the Buddha's name causes rot in the mind... So there are times when I want to let go of everything and stop practicing. But that night I had a dream and saw Buddha Shakyamuni Buddha saying:}
{align:justify|- You must be patient! The West has Ultimate Bliss, there is Amitabha Buddha! Having finished speaking, he pointed... I immediately saw Amitabha Buddha shining a bright golden light towards me. In the middle, large golden letters appeared, with the words written on them: The West has Ultimate Bliss! The West has Amitabha Buddha!}
{align:justify|Here, I want to say: cause and effect are not false. The Diamond Sutra once recorded: Tathagata's words are true words, real words, no different words! - That's true.}
{align:justify|Today I am telling these things, according to Buddha's teachings, they should not be said, but because I see a lot of sentient beings studying Buddha who only focus on form without actually practicing, my heart is very painful.}
{align:justify|Buddha dharma is not easy to meet, it is not easy to hear, it is also difficult to obtain a human body, anyone who can hear or know Buddha dharma... It can be said that for many lifetimes, they have planted mature good roots so they can meet the Buddha Dharma. Having met you, you should practice well to repay Buddha's kindness.}
{align:justify|May this merit dedicating merit to all, pray for all wronged bondholders and harmed sentient beings, in this life their hatred will be eliminated, their blessings will increase, and they will soon be reborn in good ways.}
{align:justify|Layman Vien Chieu}
{align:justify|Female scholar Vien's recitation of the Ksitigarbha Sutra achieved results very quickly, because she did not initiate any distracting thoughts. When she came to the place where Quang Muc saved her mother, she was moved by her great vows, tears flowed profusely, and her heart cut like a knife when thinking of her parents. This is filial piety and sympathy with the feelings of the Quang Muc girl, so Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara evoked a dream, clearly describing the current situation of her parents. This is the reason why some people just recite a few sets and immediately feel the response, while others do not see anything at all, it depends on whether they are sincere enough or not.}
{align:justify|The interesting point is that the Ksitigarbha Sutra praises Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva and explains his merits and vows, but this time the Bodhisattva who dreamed was not Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva, but Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara, proving that the Bodhisattvas are always interconnected, without distinction, pushing responsibilities like ordinary people.}
{align:justify|Buddha entrusted the sentient beings of the Saha world to Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva and asked Bodhisattva to save sentient beings from falling into the evil realms until Bodhisattva Maitreya (the future Buddha) descended to earth. This is an extremely difficult responsibility. Yet Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva still promised…}
{align:justify|Buddha once confirmed: He and the Bodhisattvas transformed into hundreds, thousands, and millions of bodies... enter the Saha world to save sentient beings. Surely Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva must continue to save sentient beings as promised to Buddha, but the best way to help sentient beings not fall into evil realms is to help them understand cause and effect to practice the Dharma correctly and know how to protect themselves.}
{align:justify|However, when we are exposed to the Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva incarnation, we are still unaware and do not recognize it. But it is also very easy to recognize Bodhisattva, because anyone who meets him or is far away and receives his teachings, all have one thing in common: Strong awareness, diligent practice, courageous vow to stop evil and practice good, abandon salty vegetarian diet, strictly adhere to precepts, blocking the path to falling into evil right in this life.}
{align:justify|ICH TAY'S SISTER}
{align:justify|This article is the original work of A Minh, of Tibetan Buddhism. It's about a woman who commits suicide. Normally, people who commit suicide fall into hell, but the female character here not only does not fall into hell but also reincarnates as a man. I would like to pass it on to you as research material.}
{align:justify|In Buddhist precepts, suicide is not only prohibited, but also emphasized: Suicide is an extremely serious crime. A person who commits suicide has a lot of pain in his body and mind when he dies, creating hatred... Because of these thoughts, after committing suicide: If your blessings are thin, you will fall into hell and experience great suffering.}
{align:justify|Those who commit suicide in this life have sown the seeds of suicide in their store of consciousness, creating a habit, so they have the habit of committing suicide, making it very easy for them to repeat the act of suicide in the future, and moreover, every life will be punished with many diseases and a short life for not knowing how to value the life they once had.}
{align:justify|In this article, the person who committed suicide is Ich Tay's sister. Since his sister discovered a tumor in her chest, when she went to the hospital for a check-up, it was a malignant tumor in the early stages and required surgery. But because the hospital was not qualified, the surgery was not successful and also led to severe inflammation, after which the disease spread violently. After being treated for a while, his sister could no longer bear the pain and suffering, and because of this illness, the family's finances became even more difficult. In the end, she hanged herself to death.}
{align:justify|Ich Tay every time he recounts this story, he seems very sad. He invited many Tibetan and Han monks, continuously chanting sutras to pray for his sister's passing.}
{align:justify|Because Ich Tay and I have a good relationship and are fortunate to know many people with supernatural powers, he has asked them many times about his sister's reincarnation.}
{align:justify|As a result, each time the question was asked, the answers were surprisingly similar. There were a few times I witnessed it with my own eyes. Because I want to give you reference material, I don't mind being clumsy and superficial, so I would like to write it down here to share.}
{align:justify|Because this happened a long time ago, it's difficult to recount all the details, but the main point is that this is completely true, thousands of truths!}
{align:justify|Lần thưa hỏi vị thần thông thứ nhất:}
{align:justify|I know this female Lama, so I asked her for an appointment to bring Ich Tay to meet him and help him clear up his questions. Even though Ich Tay has heard my introduction, I still have some doubts about his abilities. After meeting, after a while of questioning, he believed that this person really had supernatural powers. So he asked about his sister's reincarnation.}
{align:justify|After a period of observation, this nun clearly described the situation of his sister's reincarnation. Even though I was there, it's been so long that I've forgotten all the details.}
{align:justify|I just remember that this person said that Ich Tay's sister had reincarnated into a family of six people, currently a two-year-old boy, and also clearly described how many rooms the house had, not a high-rise house, built on a mountainside and there was a river nearby, she described it very carefully.}
{align:justify|Hearing that, Ich Tay half believed and half doubted. Because when his sister died, the family did not have time to tell him the news, it took him a long time to know. Ich Tay thought that his sister had hanged herself to death, and for 49 days, her family did not invite Venerable Cao Monk to deliver, so naturally she must go to hell, there is no way that she would not go to hell but also be reincarnated as a man.}
{align:justify|I then argued:}
{align:justify|- Even though he knew the bad news of her passing very late, he still tried his best to chant sutras to pray for her, so thanks to that she was saved. Moreover, the age of the reincarnated child is very consistent with the time after his sister passed away.}
{align:justify|But Ich Tay still refused to admit it. He insisted that he was not good at practicing, and that even if he chanted sutras to pray for rebirth, it wouldn't have that much power.}
{align:justify|I object: People chanting sutras may have poor merit, but the power of Mahayana scriptures is boundless, moreover, karma cannot be said or predicted, your sister did not go to hell but reincarnated as a man is not an unbelievable story. Moreover, I also invited the Sangha Han and Tibetan to pray for me...}
{align:justify|But Ich Tay is still hesitant.}
{align:justify|Lần hỏi thứ hai:}
{align:justify|Two years later, Ich Tay and I asked a wizard Lama Kien Tan again.}
{align:justify|This man, after a period of observation, gave the same answer as what the female Lama had previously said, but he described it more meticulously. The difference is that the boy is now two years older (because Ich Tay asked again two years later).}
{align:justify|This time Ich Tay was very excited, he had begun to believe about his sister's reincarnation situation, but he still told me: You must ask a Master who practices Vajra Vehicle to observe it for you again, then you can feel at ease.}
{align:justify|Lần thứ ba: Invite the famous living Buddha Kagyu to dream and observe.}
{align:justify|We are acquainted with a famous lama in a neighboring district. In his previous life, he was an extremely famous Rimpoche in Tibet that almost everyone knows. Although in his previous life he had extremely profound knowledge, he was famous for his supreme supernatural powers.}
{align:justify|In this life he was reincarnated, leaving the home life to study the Dharma and practice, his salvation career is extremely prolific, still showing many miraculous stories.}
{align:justify|Ich Tay and I have a very good relationship with him, moreover, the first time Ich Tay came to visit the Master, the night before he had a dream of a good omen.}
{align:justify|We stayed at the Master's place for several months, studying Tibetan together and helping him with Chinese.}
{align:justify|One day, Ich Tay gathered all his courage and asked the Master about his sister's reincarnation.}
{align:justify|It must be said that Ich Tay has a very good fate, so he receives special attention from the Master. That night he entered a dream to observe...}
{align:justify|In the morning, he ordered the attendant to call Ich Tay and I into his room and gently narrate the reincarnation situation of Ich Tay, basically the same as the previous two times.}
{align:justify|Is it different? The Master explained further for Ich Tay to understand: Because the boy (his sister's reincarnation) committed suicide in his previous life, he will have to endure many illnesses and a short life in this life. Therefore, Ich Tay needs to chant sutras and release a lot of life to dedictate merit for her, with luck to be able to resolve that unfavorable situation.}
{align:justify|Finally, the Master said, his sister's place of reincarnation lived very close to Ich Tay's house. He smiled and asked Ich Tay:}
{align:justify|- Do you want to go find the boy who is your reincarnated sister?}
{align:justify|This time, Ich Tay completely believed in his sister's reincarnation into the good world. Furthermore, he also developed infinite faith in the Master. He asked to receive teachings and study the Dharma with him.}
{align:justify|The Master then examined Ich Tay's roots and causes, then taught him the extraordinary "Yudhi" Dharma, then he introduced him to receive teachings from a lama of great perfection.}
{align:justify|Unexpectedly, the teacher Ich Tay came to receive Dharma from was monk Kien Tan.}
{align:justify|Actually, there are several other Masters who have also clarified this matter, but I can only tell you this much.}
{align:justify|SUICIDE TO THE EVIL REALM}
{align:justify|Master Dac-ni is recognized as a supreme incarnation, highly elaborate, with great achievements. During his youth, he spent a long time in seclusion and practiced asceticism, confirming full awakening in his previous life. On the outside he seemed like a crazy person, but he had enough magical powers to be free. He often brings Dharma to benefit sentient beings. Even though he has supernatural powers, he does not show them carelessly. Only when he carefully observes the conditions does he practice compassion and benefit.}
{align:justify|So, even though many people asked him to observe the future or other causes and conditions, he often gently refused, using the excuse that he was an ordinary person, not familiar with the affairs of the three lifetimes, and explained that it was all due to past karma that had ripened to bear fruit, and needed to be calmly accepted... and sincerely pray to the Three Jewels to bless all without fear.}
{align:justify|But when he encounters superior causes and conditions, he will reveal them at his own opportunity to benefit sentient beings.}
{align:justify|Now I would like to briefly record what I personally witnessed, the scene of him using profound wisdom to observe the cause and effect of three generations... to share with everyone.}
{align:justify|In early June 2000, he was invited to China to propagate the Dharma, staying for a few days in Chengdu. Countless followers came to worship and ask for advice. He is not tired and always gives them satisfaction.}
{align:justify|One afternoon, a middle-aged Ms.}
{align:justify|She said that in 1994, due to a family argument, her mother drank poison and committed suicide. At that time, she did not know Buddha's teachings and had not taken refuge in the Three Jewels. Because he didn't understand the religion, he couldn't deliver it to his mother in time. A few years later, she took refuge in the Three Jewels, studied Buddha's teachings, and learned that most people who commit suicide end up in hell. Therefore, she was extremely worried, so she begged him to observe the deliverance for her.}
{align:justify|After I finished translating for you, you taught:}
{align:justify|- I am an ordinary person, I cannot observe your mother's current whereabouts. But if you release five hundred lives, I will assist you in cultivating dedicating merit, so the dead can be reborn in a good world.}
{align:justify|Miss}
{align:justify|Perhaps thanks to his filial piety, the Great Master suddenly blurted out a explanation for her mother's reincarnation.}
{align:justify|It turns out that her Indian mother, after committing suicide, immediately fell into the evil realm and was born as a poisonous snake. So through many lifetimes of birth, death and death... She is still a poisonous snake, she has never separated from the snake body.}
{align:justify|Later, thanks to her family asking the Sangha to deliver the blessing, her mother, in a short time, temporarily escaped the life of a single snake and was reincarnated into a good realm. But due to her lack of good roots and not knowing the Buddha's practice, she continued to fall as a solitary snake. Just carry the snake body back and forth many times.}
{align:justify|This time, the Great Master especially promised to chant sutras to bless and support her rebirth Pure Land. He also advised Ms. Releasing animals, chanting sutras… dedicating merit to mother.}
{align:justify|I translated what he taught to the lady. She was very grateful and confirmed: What the monk said about her mother was very true.}
{align:justify|Because, when her mother passed away, she had not yet taken refuge. It was not until 2005 that she began to take refuge. After taking refuge, she organized many times at temples in Hanoi to pray for her mother's death.}
{align:justify|After that, she often dreamed that her mother appeared very miserable. That's why I'm always worried and uneasy.}
{align:justify|Recently, she had a dream like this: At first I saw myself and my mother walking on the avenue, then I didn't see my mother, I only saw a great python laying eggs on the side of the road.}
{align:justify|After waking up from the dream, her heart became even more uneasy and panicked, fearing that her mother had fallen into the body of a snake.}
{align:justify|This time, when she heard that the Master was temporarily staying in Chengdu, she took the liberty to come and ask for advice. Unexpectedly, I was lucky enough to hear him tell the story of my mother's reincarnation. For this kindness, she is extremely grateful and has increased faith.}
{align:justify|She promised to follow his teachings, try to bring happiness to her mother and ask for the Master's instructions, follow him and practice well, to soon escape samsara and benefit sentient beings.}
{align:justify|Those who had the good fortune to be present there, after listening to the Great Master's teachings, all developed faith in him and the cause and effect of the three generations, vowed to follow him, practice the Dharma and practice.}
{align:justify|What I have recorded here, all of which have been witnessed by lay people at the scene, is true and not false.}
{align:justify|Explanation further:}
{align:justify|There are books written by people who open the heavenly eye (in the West and the East), they tell about the state of a person who commits suicide after death, very tragically, with many similarities. If the person who commits suicide knows the harsh suffering that awaits them, they will certainly not dare to seek death.}
{align:justify|A person who commits suicide, after death, must receive a hundred times more suffering than when he was alive. Of course, usually they have to fall into hell. But because their positive life has not yet ended, the retribution they have to pay in this life has not yet been completed, so the retributions pile up and they have to bear it themselves, not to mention the additional sins of impiety and self-destruction.}
{align:justify|After the person who committed suicide was sentenced, the devil immediately took him to the place where they committed suicide. If their life expectancy is 70 and they committed suicide at 40, they must return to the place where they committed suicide and re-enact this act every day. Those who jump from buildings must re-enact the act of jumping from buildings every day at that location, meaning they must re-enact their act of committing suicide for thirty years, until the end of their lifespan, then they can leave this place and return to hell to receive retribution. When their life is over, they will become animals or abnormal or disabled people. Moreover, they are also haunted by the karma of suicide from the past, making them like to commit suicide for life and life. This is very scary, because the seeds of suicide have followed and are deeply ingrained in their consciousness, so ten thousand times you should not commit suicide, because you will suffer for thousands of lifetimes and it will be difficult to recover.}
{align:justify|Lama () Dinh Qua Kham once said: When a person chooses to commit suicide, other than having their consciousness follow evil karma, they have absolutely no other choice, not to mention they can be controlled by evil spirits, using their life force.}
{align:justify|When living, most people think: Death is the end, the end, liberation from all suffering. They are completely unaware that after committing suicide they will suffer fiercely, and at this point it will be too late to regret.}
{align:justify|Those who commit suicide have a very difficult time getting a chance to be born as a human. Because human life is difficult to obtain, they do not know how to cherish it, they seek death, they give up their human body, they give up the opportunity to live a virtuous and honest life, they give up the nurturing care of their parents. People who commit suicide also cause many negative effects on the human world, so they are often reborn in the animal world, where it is not easy to take on a human body.}
{align:justify|Buddha DIRECTIONS PLEASE WORK}
{align:justify|I have been studying Buddhism for several years. Because my son recently got sick, I took him everywhere for treatment, but to no avail. Later, I happened to go online and saw the website "Son Tay Minor Institute" of Buddhism, so I asked for a copy of the Ksitigarbha sutra to take home and read, hoping that maybe I would find good medicine that could save my child.}
{align:justify|However, after just turning a few pages, I found it too difficult, because there was a lot of text, and it was in traditional Chinese, and there were also descriptions of many types of demons and gods that were completely contrary to the atheism and concepts of the modern world that I had learned in school.}
{align:justify|I didn't understand the sutras, so I really wanted to hear their explanation, so I went online to find Dharma Master Tinh Khong's website to explain the sutras, and since then I've benefited a lot.}
{align:justify|The most obvious thing is that my health has improved better. Previously, I followed the weight loss and dieting movement, but did not lose weight, but also made my stomach, intestines... Unstable, hot inside, urinary retention, no energy, very bad health.}
{align:justify|chanting sutras After a few years, I saw my health getting better, especially my son's illness. When I was in the city, I couldn't cure his cramps. When I returned to my hometown, I happened to meet an extremely kind Oriental medicine doctor. After nearly a year of diagnosis, the boy's condition recovered nine-tenths of the time. This is also the motivation that makes me more persistent in studying Buddha.}
{align:justify|This year, for personal reasons, I quit my job and stayed home for nearly six months. Then I decided to look for a new job. But someone like me who doesn't have professional forte, is middle-aged, and has no talent that surpasses the younger generation, so I have the feeling that if I'm not smart, I will be eliminated by society.}
{align:justify|Because in 2008 and 2009, talented junior generations appeared, so it was not easy for a middle-aged woman like me to find a suitable job.}
{align:justify|Fortunately, I was able to listen to Buddha's teachings and meet a teacher, so I understood that everything is cause and effect, so I can put aside my worries and live happily.}
{align:justify|While going online, I happened to see that other Dharma friends and brothers also posted ads looking for jobs, it was very interesting, strange and interesting, so I followed suit and drafted my own "Job Seeking Application" as follows:}
{align:justify|I really hope to find a job that meets the standards:}

{align:justify|I wrote a simple job application, because I don't think I have any blessings, so I don't dare to ask for much, I just hope to have a job close to home, have time to take care of my family and study, which is precious.}
{align:justify|After I finished writing the job application, I followed the prescribed coursework and practiced it. If there is a recruitment announcement, it will be found online.}
{align:justify|Two weeks have passed, no results yet. In the third week, I saw a job advertisement on the internet, but after reviewing the conditions, I found it wasn't suitable for me so I didn't apply.}
{align:justify|A few days passed, a certain unit announced a recruitment, I mustered up the courage to write a "Job Application" and send it. Unexpectedly, the company responded, inviting me to meet for a try. Then I went to work like I do now. 9 a.m. in the morning, 5 p.m. in the afternoon, the work place is about 45 minutes drive from home, just like my wish, because this is the work of helping people, belonging to right livelihood, right karma. I remember what Master Tinh Khong once said: In Buddhism, "If you ask for it, it will come true". If the demand is not met, the problem is with us. I've been working for two months now.}
{align:justify|Thank you all Buddhas, Bodhisattva, Long, Thien, Thien Than, thank you Dharma Masters for wholeheartedly teaching me.}
{align:justify|Disciple of the Three Jewels - January 10, 2016}
{align:justify|WIVE'S CONFIDENCE}
{align:justify|This autobiography is by Vien Vien, a member of the Upper Lotus Center. She had previously experienced extreme suffering. After that, fortunately meeting a wise friend, she developed a repentance mind, practiced, corrected her mistakes and gradually trained her mind. Up to now, she has completely changed and been "reborn".}
{align:justify|The following is her story:}

{align:justify|When I was a young woman at home, I lived a very ungrateful life. Because my father has a hot temper, when he's happy he behaves well with my mother and me, but when he gets angry, he doesn't hit me but instead yells and scolds me... Makes me feel unsafe. The mind is always suppressed. That's why I often avoid my father. I rarely talked to him, whenever I saw him I immediately avoided him. I never thought about my father's feelings, never knowing that this would hurt and upset him.}
{align:justify|Later, from Anhui, I moved to Shanghai to live and met my current husband. At first, we texted each other every day and spent a lot of time chatting on the phone. Their love grew closer and closer, and after a year they got married.}
{align:justify|After getting married, I live with my husband's parents. After initially going through the polite stage, the atmosphere of tyranny, aggression, oppression, suspicion... started surrounding me.}
{align:justify|My husband is busy at work and doesn't come home until late at night. I'm as suspicious as Cao Cao, so I'm constantly calling him.}
{align:justify|Now that I think about it, this is also because I grew up in a family that felt unsafe, plus I did not understand Buddha's teachings, was used to being immersed in ignorance, and did not know how to consciously control the ego.}
{align:justify|I was very lazy at that time, when I got home from work I worried about sleeping, sleeping until it was time to eat, I was still unhappy.}
{align:justify|Personally, whenever I give something, I always want to receive it back. If I don't get anything, I hold on to my troubles.}
{align:justify|Once I even went to my husband's company to tell the story, never thinking that doing so would create a negative impact on his company. My husband was very angry, adding to the accumulation of previous conflicts, making it very difficult for him, the result: This is the first time he asked for a divorce.}
{align:justify|Of course I don't agree, although on the outside I pretend to be humble and patient, but inside I am very angry, feeling that they (my husband's family) are all at fault with me. Since you married me, why don't you let me be happy? My face was sad all day, especially every time I saw my mother-in-law, I wanted to immediately run back to my room and close the door.}
{align:justify|When eating, my husband has the hardest time, because he has to sit between two women who are fighting each other, so his face is very unsightly. That's why he comes home later and later, often away, traveling... more and more, making the resentment in my heart grow stronger.}
{align:justify|After being married for more than a year, I gave birth to a daughter. This should have been a happy thing, but my painful days began again. Because in every situation, I always look in the bad direction.}
{align:justify|My mother-in-law took care of me during my stay. She had a nervous breakdown and often had insomnia at night. Father-in-law still has to go to work, so housework, holding grandchildren, cooking... It's all her concern. I still resent her for not taking care of her grandchildren at night.}
{align:justify|The month of maternity leave is over, I'm taking care of my child, and I feel even more like my mother-in-law wants to cause trouble for me everywhere. Whenever I watch TV, she deliberately leans over to not let me watch. After I change my child's clothes, she deliberately changes him into another outfit. Now that I think back, there really was nothing wrong with what my mother-in-law did, it was all because I was too sensitive, too suspicious, and subjectively interpreted it myself.}
{align:justify|At that time, every time I went home to visit my biological parents, I always complained that my mother-in-law and husband were not good to me. My mother loves her daughter, so she defends me and grits her teeth to blame them. My father, who was nearby, also became angry.}
{align:justify|When my child was six months old, I wanted to go to work and gave the child to my mother-in-law. Because I didn't want to meet my mother-in-law, I kept "going home early in the evening", my husband and children did not care, and finally one day: Conflict broke out, my mother-in-law saw that I was not taking care of the family all day, nor taking care of my children. She could no longer bear it, so she came to my house to scold me. Because I had previously complained about my husband's family, as soon as my mother-in-law entered the door, my mother got angry, argued with her, and made so much noise that things were thrown out. This conflict opened the door for my husband to stand up for my mother. He firmly requested a divorce and also forbade me to stay in their house.}
{align:justify|I rented a house alone outside, my daughter couldn't see me, my husband didn't come, I also had to face the questioning and anger of my parents.}
{align:justify|At that time, I felt regret in my heart, so I apologized to my husband. My husband is very good, he gives me money to rent a room and lets me see my daughter every weekend. Now that I think back, I see that he and my mother-in-law were truly compassionate, tolerant and generous!}
{align:justify|Only this time, no matter how much I begged, he still insisted on a divorce. Every day I was alone in the rented room, crying, only sleeping three or four hours a day, sleeping when I was tired, then waking up and continuing to cry, wetting the pillow. I miss my daughter, my heart hurts like a knife, my hair has turned a lot gray in just a few months.}

{align:justify|Immersed in extreme confusion and suffering, I suddenly remembered Bodhisattva Avalokitesvara's salvation, so I rushed to the temple, worshiped His compassion statue, and then invited a small statue of Him to worship. Every day stand before Him and worship. At that time, I completely did not understand what it means to truly practice according to Buddha's teachings. I only thought that bowing before Him like that meant believing in Buddha and He would bless me.}
{align:justify|Unexpectedly, for someone like me who understands the shallow teachings of Buddha's teachings, Bodhisattva also took pity on him. Three months later, my husband listened to the advice of his friends and did not ask for a divorce anymore.}
{align:justify|At that time, although I had regrets and was happy because my wish had come true, in my heart there were still many things I was not willing to do, and I still felt like I was a victim, a young daughter-in-law who was bullied and kicked out of the house by her husband.}
{align:justify|I rented a house outside for about three years. During these three years, my husband also lived in two places. The details here are difficult to describe.}
{align:justify|After three years, my husband's old house was demolished, cleared, and resettled, so we were divided into one house. At that time I thought: Now I can finally no longer have to live with my mother-in-law.}
{align:justify|I don't see my mother-in-law's hair turning white, her haggard figure, her thin body, for what she has sacrificed for her son. At that time I thought that all my misfortunes were caused by her!}
{align:justify|So I created all kinds of trouble for myself. With that mindset, tragedy is bound to happen.}
{align:justify|During the renovation of the new house, my husband let me manage and take care of it. But I don't care, I'm just staring at one thing: Is my name written on the house documents? My husband said that if he wanted to get the house papers done, the internal and external communication costs would cost tens of thousands. He doesn't have enough money right now, so he advised me to wait a few years before getting the papers done, there's no need to rush. I was very angry when I heard him say that. I started to doubt him. I didn't bother to cook for him. During the cold war every day, my daughter didn't even bother to take care of him. All I could think about was: "If you don't do the house paperwork, it means you don't really want to live with me." The more I thought about it, the angrier I became, filled with sadness, it seemed like the anger caused me to get breast cancer. When I went to the doctor, the cells had mutated and had to be treated with chemotherapy. The doctor said, if it is delayed for six months, it will be difficult to treat.}
{align:justify|One time my husband wanted to eat rice but I didn't bother to cook it, so there was a conflict. He couldn't bear it anymore and hit me. I immediately reported to the police. After that, the more I thought about it, the angrier I became, so I went to the "Women's Association" to complain about my mother-in-law. Because I didn't think about the consequences, in my anger, I went to a television station to advertise on a reconciliation program, complaining about all sorts of things against my mother-in-law, causing a very bad influence and reputation for my mother-in-law.}
{align:justify|Now that I think back, it's true that at that time I was no better than an animal. When my husband and I first met, he advised me to study accounting and arranged for me to go to his relative's company to study, helping me know bookkeeping well.}
{align:justify|After getting married, he sponsored me to study at University of Finance. Afterwards, thanks to my mother-in-law helping to take care of the children, I devoted myself to studying and succeeding.}
{align:justify|When my biological mother had a stomach tumor, my husband helped her get admitted to the hospital, find a good doctor for treatment, buy medicine (buying medicine at that time was difficult, even if she had money, it was difficult to buy it), my mother-in-law also helped me find a room to rent at a discount so that my parents could leave the hospital and live in peace. They are all great kindnesses, but I treat them like this...}

{align:justify|Due to the issue of house registration papers and my daughter's schooling, I had constant disputes with my husband, combined with previous resentments and injustices, so in anger, without thinking about the consequences, I went to Court to file for divorce. When my husband received the summons, he immediately sought me out to discuss it, but I avoided him and didn't bother to talk to him.}
{align:justify|Looking back now, I was truly ignorant at that time. Because I always feel insecure, combined with my self-centered nature, I actually need money, a house, children, and I don't want a divorce. I just want my husband to care about me and listen to me.}
{align:justify|During that time, I really felt like living was worse than dying, thinking back that I used to be a pure girl, and was oppressed by the whole family to turn into this!}
{align:justify|But why has it come to this? How is that right? Deep down in my heart, I had a feeling that what I was doing was wrong, but I couldn't find the answer.}
{align:justify|In the pain and confusion, I went to Bodhisattva temple again, just like before, I kept bowing my head, praying to Bodhisattva for help and guidance to break the delusion.}
{align:justify|This time I go one step further: Connect with the Buddha Sutra. A heavenly book that is not a Buddhist scripture, right there attracts me, with an elegant lotus flower on the cover. I really like it, it's the book "The First Lotus of the Heart" volume six.}
{align:justify|Each story in the book captivated me, making me read it over and over again. Especially here is an article by a wife in the same situation as me, expressing her feelings of awakening and seeing her own mistakes. I feel like I'm inferior to that other wife, because her reflection is really profound... I thought about what I had done, and my conscience began to awaken.}
{align:justify|After returning home, I sat and reflected on myself for a while, then burst into tears. This time I'm not crying because I'm wronged, but because I feel like I've wronged you too much, really too much!}
{align:justify|I am an ungrateful person, what people do for me is always taken for granted, I live without responsibility to my biological parents and my husband's parents. A child who fails to be filial, a wife who fails to fulfill her duties... From any angle I look at it, I'm not good!}
{align:justify|When I realized I was so wrong, I hastily withdrew the lawsuit. But it was too late. As soon as I withdrew the application, my husband also filed a lawsuit and firmly told me: You have forgiven me countless times, have been patient with me countless times, you have endured enough, so you are determined to divorce.}
{align:justify|Now everything seemed hopeless, I felt like I was in too much pain, no one could understand or sympathize with me, so on the day of the trial, I took a dose of sleeping pills, wrote a suicide note, and then lay on the bed and passed out.}
{align:justify|Before the time of suicide, I was guided and guided by Senior Sister Lieu to get married to the Ksitigarbha Sutra, chanting it every day, hoping that Bodhisattva would be compassionate and not abandon me. At the same time, I also tried to join the Lien Hoa team. On the last day, I expressed my thoughts of leaving this world.}
{align:justify|Then I learned: During the two days I was in a coma, the Dharma friends in the team always chanted Buddha's name and dedicated it to me. My close colleagues and friends saw that I hadn't come to work for two days and couldn't contact me, so they were worried and came to my house to visit... discovered that I was unconscious, so he quickly took me to the emergency hospital. It was true that the Buddhas and Bodhisattvas never abandoned me, thanks to that I was saved.}
{align:justify|A few days before I committed suicide, I sent money to release animals to the Lotus group, perhaps thanks to my good will to open a path to life for animals, but invisibly also opened a path to life for myself.}

{align:justify|My husband requested to prosecute the divorce, but because I committed suicide, it was postponed. But whatever happens has to happen, it can't be because I really realized the mistake that I could fix it right away. At the court, no matter how much I cried and begged, my husband was still as cold as ice, without the slightest emotion. He bluntly said that he no longer had any feelings for me. His cold words and icy eyes made me cry even more.}
{align:justify|I firmly did not agree to divorce. At that time, the court did not rule on divorce, only told me: It's useless to try to hold on to me. If I had known this day would exist, I wouldn't have done it in the first place.}
{align:justify|That day I cried until I got home, I kept crying, I cried until I couldn't cry anymore, so I lay dead on the bed and moaned.}
{align:justify|During this time I was living alone in the new house, my husband and children lived with my husband's family. My husband hardly talked to me. No matter what you say, it's just a request for divorce. I can only see my daughter once a weekend. My spirit and health are extremely bad: His face was gloomy, without any vitality. Every time my daughter calls to say "missing mom", I cry until I don't have the strength to cry anymore. At night, I often have trouble sleeping. Even when I sleep, I always have nightmares. When I wake up, I start crying again.}
{align:justify|During the day I always fall into worry and sadness, every time I think I remember the wrong things I did in the past, I can't help but tremble all over my body, I can't breathe, I'm sweating profusely, I don't want to go out the door, I'm very afraid of meeting people... My whole body and mind are tormented by shame, unable to imagine that I can continue to live in the future.}
{align:justify|The thing that touches me the most is that, even though I am so evil, all Buddhas and Bodhisattva are still compassionate and do not abandon a sentient being struggling in suffering like me, and are still determined to save me. My close friends and monks did not leave me, and compassionately helped me. The Dharma friends in the Upper Lotus Center team did not abandon me or be afraid of bothering me. On the contrary, they were very patient and guided me.}
{align:justify|Under the guidance of my fellow Buddhists, I tried my best to correct and innovate, started chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras, chanting them every day, and also copying them, bowing to King Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva, and writing down the insights that thanks to chanting the sutras my mind was transformed. Before all Buddhas, Bodhisattva I sincerely repent, repentance my mistakes, making vows to correct and innovate.}
{align:justify|When I reminisce about my past unfilial mistakes, I am immersed in sadness that I can't get out of, I can't even chant sutras. My Dharma friends advise me that the mistakes of the past are beyond repair and the current cause and effect has already punished me.}
{align:justify|Here, I especially want to thank my Dharma friends in the Lien Hoa team, especially Sister To Tam. During my extremely miserable days, Sister To Tam always stood by my side, sharing her practice experience at her mother-in-law's house, to encourage and cheer me, giving me great and incomparable support. If it weren't for you, I probably wouldn't have been able to change this quickly.}
{align:justify|Ms. To Tam taught me to start correcting from the smallest details in life. For example, the house must be cleaned, the rooms kept clean, and things that are not needed must be liquidated and given away. When I sweep the house or clean, I feel like I am cleaning my mind, sweeping away all the impurities from my mind, and then reciting Buddha's name will purify it.}
{align:justify|There was also a Dharma friend who advised me to read Lieu Pham Tu Hoi, telling me to let all my mistakes die with yesterday, to see today as a new day starting. That although the power of karma is great, the compassionate vow power of all Buddhas and Bodhisattva is even greater. Bring the feeling of gratitude to all Buddhas and Bodhisattva with you, so that when traveling, sitting in the car, cooking, cooking or cleaning... That is, no matter what you do, at any moment, you must silently recite Buddha's name, you should act in accordance with the kindness and wisdom of all Buddhas, Bodhisattva and vow to bring this field of blessing and dedicating merit to sentient beings.}
{align:justify|That's it, step by step, step by step… I practice this good habit, my mind gradually changes. I am truly aware: Harming others is harming yourself. Wanting to correct my ancient selfish notions. I am not impatient, hasty, do not consider myself to be the center, always put myself in the position of others to sympathize, understand, be tolerant, patient, and hard-working with others. I often observe and check my inner errors. Whenever I have a bad thought, I immediately repentance to eliminate it immediately. Let go of ego, learn and practice according to the compassion and wisdom of all Buddhas, Bodhisattva, everywhere, think for others, learn how to live: Know how to be grateful and repay...}

{align:justify|Thinking back carefully, I did a lot of things wrong in the past.}
{align:justify|As a child, you are not filial, do not care for your parents, as a daughter-in-law you often clash with your mother-in-law, and as a wife you are not gentle. Right now I need to fulfill my duty, and even do it thoughtfully and excellently.}
{align:justify|First I have to make amends with my family, then I don't care about divorce or not. No matter what my husband decides, I have to correct my mistakes, innovate, and improve myself, not because I want to not divorce. Because in the past I did wrong and brought a lot of suffering to the people around me, so I want to atone for my sins by reforming myself. No matter what, I must fulfill my responsibilities. If our fate has ended and you want to divorce, then I will accommodate and sincerely wish you happiness.}
{align:justify|My mind has calmed down, I no longer have attachments or want to be private, gradually the worries that bind me become less and less. In the past, every day around 3 o'clock in the afternoon, my mind would collapse and feel sad, wanting to cry, going crazy, even wanting to commit suicide. Now these negative thoughts become less and less. Until the new year, there is no more. At night, I no longer had insomnia or had nightmares, but slept very well, making my friends and the Master around me compliment me on my strange change to the point that I was almost no longer the same as before, and my appearance also became more beautiful. At work, I treat the company, colleagues... More attentive, enthusiastic and hardworking, very good relationship. Regarding work, I feel very comfortable. In daily life, I feel more and more filled with love, gratitude, and compassion.}
{align:justify|But the process of correcting my errors sounds easy, but in reality I often have to practice doing it over and over again. Because if I'm just a little bit careless, I'll lose my awareness and my confused habit will erupt just like before and cause me to do something wrong. There was a time when I was so deep in attachment, so deep in pain that I couldn't raise my head. At those times, I was very depressed, so I asked Ms. To Tam to help me solve it.}
{align:justify|In the beginning, I once texted my husband for a long time without receiving a response. I then sank into the abyss of sadness. Ms. To Tam advised me to believe in all Buddhas, Bodhisattva, she told me to recite the Heart Sutra 21 times to stop false thoughts, to follow Buddha's teachings and do my duty as a daughter, daughter-in-law, good wife...}
{align:justify|I also went to my parents' house to repentance with my father because he had previously behaved indifferently, making him sad. I cried, my father also cried. I said I was unfilial, knowing my mistakes. Please forgive me.}
{align:justify|My father said it's good to know I'm wrong, he forgives me. Currently, my parents and I have a very good relationship. Father's irritability also improved a lot.}
{align:justify|I texted my husband and mother-in-law, thanking them for their great kindness, thanking them for taking care of my daughter, and instructing them to repent of their mistakes.}
{align:justify|Of course my husband's side couldn't accept it right away, I understood "The ice is three meters thick, it's hard to melt quickly in the morning or afternoon". Because I hurt them too deeply before.}
{align:justify|At first, every weekend when I came to pick up my daughter, my mother-in-law wouldn't let me in. As for the gifts I bought to give, she left them outside the door. At that time I thought: Even though my mother-in-law beat me, scolded me, or threw things at me, I still did not give up and continued to give gifts... Because everything I do now is to redeem and apologize... that's all.}
{align:justify|Gradually, my mother-in-law called to tell me to buy this and that (things needed for her daughter's studies). On weekends, when my husband came to pick up the children, he also stopped by the house to watch a little TV. Even if you don't talk to me or eat the food I cook, I'm still very grateful.}
{align:justify|I always keep the house clean, when you come I always make you hot tea and serve it to you. Since he often goes to work, I told him to leave his dirty clothes for me to wash (explaining that Mom was already working very hard, so it would be more convenient for me to do it).}

{align:justify|When in my heart I no longer claim my own rights, I wholeheartedly care for others, I only want to express my gratitude, I just want to do something for others, this behavior has completely changed my inner self and people can also feel my heart.}
{align:justify|At the end of this year, my husband came by, of course not to eat but to have a New Year's party with his uncle, he also did not invite me. I'm not angry, I even made delicious cakes to give as gifts.}
{align:justify|After that, I stayed home alone, cleaned the house, and waited for him and his daughter to return from the party.}
{align:justify|A few days later, he said he wanted me to write a letter admitting his mistake and wanted me to proactively give up ownership of the house. I completely agree, moreover I am very happy, because you gave me the opportunity to repentance, I wrote it in two nights and finished it.}
{align:justify|At this time, my husband proactively said he would give me 20 percent of the property rights, but I did not request it, and confirmed that I voluntarily gave up all property rights and rooms. Before, I valued property the most, but now I really want to let go of all the material things that I used to attach great importance to. Do you know? After letting go, my heart felt extremely comfortable and light. I enjoyed an unprecedented sense of peace and joy. This is what I gained so greatly!}
{align:justify|Throughout the spring, I still persevered in doing what needed to be done, sweeping the toilet, mopping the house clean, enthusiastically preparing rice in the kitchen, I paid attention to researching delicious vegetarian dishes to cook for people. In the past, I was a lazy girl, but now, even if he just stops by, food, water, blankets, chairs, beds... I always keep it clean, regardless of whether you come to stay or not, whether you eat or not, I always make a decent tray of rice and have it ready. Over time, he also realized that I had changed and began to communicate better.}
{align:justify|One day in mid-March this year, the weather was very beautiful, he suddenly came to me to pack my luggage, explained that his friend had just bought a car, and invited our whole family to go on a trip. I obediently prepared my luggage and took my daughter with me.}
{align:justify|During the trip, he bought malt candy for me to eat, but the malt candy was too sticky so I ate it awkwardly and it was sticky, making him laugh. We had a lot of fun on the trip. My daughter is very happy, all three of us are happy, a happiness we haven't had in many years.}
{align:justify|Since that trip, he started eating the rice I cooked, and we began to interact more sympathetically. This year, on May 1, my husband and I went up the mountain together to worship Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva King. Stay in the mountain for one night. Late at night, listening to the chanting of the morning sutras in the temple, my heart suddenly felt infinite attachment to Bodhisattva...}
{align:justify|In October this year, my sister is getting married, we promised to go worship Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva.}

{align:justify|Now, in life, I can see my husband's kindness everywhere. When he was at home, he woke up early in the morning to boil hot water, make tea, put it by the window, and waited for my daughter and I to wake up and there was warm tea to drink. When my daughter and I went to brush our teeth and wash our faces, he went to fold the blankets, I told him not to fold them, I'll do it later... but he looked at me gently, having just finished folding the blanket. I'm really not up to the task of being a wife.}
{align:justify|When I casually said I liked eating durian, he immediately bought it the next day, and also bought a large lychee from Son Truc. He explains: You must eat durian with Son Truc lychee, this is good, otherwise it will be very hot.}
{align:justify|You really are such a thoughtful husband.}
{align:justify|At the same time my friends came to visit, I ate durian with them. He called from work and asked me if it was delicious? It wasn't because of the greeting, but the way he showed his caring heart that made me feel infinitely warm.}
{align:justify|Now, my mother-in-law picks up my daughter every day for me. She gives me a lot of comfort. After work, I can go do what I like. I silently thank her. My mother-in-law always calls to warn me to pay attention: What should you eat when your body is hot, what should you eat if your stomach is not comfortable? It's really like "Having an old person in a family is like having a treasure".}
{align:justify|Normally in life, my husband is very delicate, he takes care of me every little bit. Always check the car so I can drive safely. When I go to a meeting with friends, he secretly puts money in my wallet, afraid I won't have enough.}
{align:justify|On the weekend, without saying a word, he took me to the clothing store. I thought he wanted to buy clothes for me, but unexpectedly he bought them for me.}
{align:justify|On my day off, he took me out to eat delicious vegetarian food in the big city (I'm a foodie, I really enjoy nourishing my body).}
{align:justify|After eating, he took me to see a movie.}
{align:justify|Last weekend, he took me to the 46-story Dai Lau area to admire the scenery. Everything you do for me shows your warm love. I stood by the river admiring the scenery, every angle was beautiful. I saw the Pearl of the Orient, the center of Hoan Chau, the center of Shanghai, it was so beautiful. Then I looked at him, thinking that his heart was the most beautiful, more beautiful than all the beautiful scenery around here, he was so warm and full of love to me, making me feel like I was disappearing into it.}
{align:justify|This wonderful, happy family life that I have is thanks to the Buddha's Dharma, thanks to the wise men who guided me, helped me awaken, vow to change myself, develop a mind of repentance, and gratitude. Know how to see the good points in the people around you, give up petty selfishness, and understand that: In life, you should know how to give, instead of demanding to receive.}
{align:justify|Since then everything has changed, I did not expect that I would reap so many wonderful things, that I can only be amazed and endlessly happy.}
{align:justify|Currently I can only practice in my free time, because I'm busy working and taking care of my family. Even though I spent very little time on the elaborate course, my faith in the Buddha's teachings grew stronger and stronger. I no longer cling to the past to suffer, continue to study and practice Buddha Dharma, and enjoy the happiness and peace of the present.}
{align:justify|At present, for the time being, my husband still does not understand my practice and chanting sutras. Because I do not want to bother him, I often chant silently, reciting Buddha's name, reciting Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva King silently, continuing to dedicating merit to sentient beings and to the world.}
{align:justify|Add: The other day, we were doing the house paperwork, and he wrote my name in.}
{align:justify|Hopefully my story will help women in the same situation who are still immersed in ignorance and suffering... will find a way out like me.}
{align:justify|Justify: The husband here is a kind and responsible person. He did not engage in promiscuity or promiscuity during his long period of separation due to disagreements with his wife.}
{align:justify|Vien Vien wrote this autobiography in a state of complete awareness, so she always saw the advantages of her husband's family and was ready to admit her mistakes.}
{align:justify|She tasted the sweetness thanks to her sincere practice of Buddha Dharma and self-improvement. This happiness was created and inspired by herself.}
{align:justify|Here is another story told by Vien Vien:}
{align:justify|Uncle X's relationship}
{align:justify|Uncle X is my aunt's husband. X's stepmother committed suicide due to family conflicts. My aunt has a bad temper and is very cold towards my uncle. It can be said that their marriage is not compatible.}
{align:justify|At that time, my uncle really wanted to divorce, but after hearing a friend say that because of his divorce, his son committed suicide. So my uncle didn't divorce because he was worried about his son. Wait until you're an adult before you divorce.}
{align:justify|My uncle and aunt divorced, fate turned around and he met his current wife.}
{align:justify|Because his next wife is a beautiful young girl, twenty years younger than his uncle, he is also afraid that if he gets married, it will not be okay, so he is very worried about this remarriage.}
{align:justify|I have a friend who is a disciple of a monk at a temple in Guangxi, and he introduced me to meet the master.}
{align:justify|The uncle took the beautiful young girl to the temple, but let his girlfriend wait outside. After he entered the temple, Master immediately said: He is doing very well, his wife is currently waiting outside.}
{align:justify|Then Master explained clearly the origin of my uncle's current relationship as follows:}
{align:justify|"About 30 years ago, when he was studying at university, one time he happened to see a drowned girl on the road. He spent ten dong to have the boatman pick her up (at that time, ten dong was a very large amount of money). Because the girl was picked up without any clothes, he immediately took off his coat and covered her, then placed her body on the side of the road, waiting for relatives to come and claim it.}
{align:justify|This girl has now transformed, she is the lady standing outside waiting for you.}
{align:justify|My uncle also told me that the current girl's appearance is very similar to the girl who drowned in the past, and her age from the year she died to her birth is also very consistent.}
{align:justify|After listening to the master explain cause and effect, my uncle felt relieved and decided to marry this beauty.}
{align:justify|Later, they had a son. He is about 50 years old, and his beautiful wife is only about thirty. They are a typical couple, an old husband and a young wife, living happily together.}
{align:justify|His uncle has a good nature, is very respectful, and his family is very rich. Even though he was divorced, he still divided the house and a lot of money with his first wife. When his wife got sick, his stepfather took care of her and took good care of her. But when my uncle got sick, my first wife didn't worry. Everything is taken care of by the second wife.}
{align:justify|When my uncle got sick, the specialists said he had cancer. Master taught me that I should release animals. Even though I didn't understand anything, I still bought many turtles to release them. It's strange to say that my uncle's illness was cured. I don't know if it has anything to do with releasing animals, but I feel that he has a very good relationship with Buddha.}
{align:justify|After he recovered, he took his wife and children to pay homage to the holy place of all Buddhas, Bodhisattva.}
{align:justify|I told my uncle's story because I wanted to talk about cause and effect, because my mother did not believe in Buddha, but because his story was so truthful, thanks to this, my mother began to believe deeply in cause and effect.}
{align:justify|Husband and wife are destined to find each other due to bad or good fate. Without fate, there will be no ending.}
{align:justify|My aunt is my first wife, but she doesn't take care of my uncle, perhaps the relationship and debt are not deep. But the next wife, out of gratitude, came to her, even though in the past her uncle only saved her body. But my uncle's kindness and kindness were still rewarded.}
{align:justify|CHILDREN'S EYES}
{align:justify|In the spring of 1976, I went to Har market to buy things and heard people talking about something that had happened not long before.}
{align:justify|There was a woman who took her grandchild on a long-distance bus to return to her hometown. After getting in the car, my grandson, about 3 or 4 years old, suddenly cried and insisted on getting out of the car. No matter what, he insisted on leaving the car. He cried more and more fiercely. The grandmother did not understand why the child kept crying loudly and wanted to get out of the car, so she advised and scolded him. But the boy didn't change his mind, he cried even more and looked terrified. Reluctantly, the grandmother had to lead the child out of the car.}
{align:justify|After leaving the car, she asked him:}
{align:justify|- Why are you crying?}
{align:justify|The boy pointed towards the car, looked horrified, and said:}
{align:justify|- The people in the car all had no heads, it scared me to death!}
{align:justify|After listening, grandmother understood: Children's eyes are pure, sometimes they see things that adults cannot see.}
{align:justify|As a result, the car had just set off and had not been running for long when it crashed straight into the river, all passengers on the car died. What the boy saw was a vision of dying ghosts.}
{align:justify|(This car accident occurred in Heilongjiang province, Mai Ly Tu town, told personally by 62-year-old Chu Ngoc Huong in May 2001).}
{align:justify|ENTERTAINMENT BUILDING}
{align:justify|In 1936, when the Japanese army had not yet occupied major cities in the country, they often sent planes to bomb Nanjing, terrifying everyone everywhere.}
{align:justify|One day, an old man over 60 took a boy about 8 or 9 years old to walk to "Thang Ky Lau", this was the entertainment area of the city at that time, meaning that in their free time, people could come here to read books, play chess, recite poetry, sing, whatever they wanted, because there was enough entertainment here. The old man took the boy upstairs to watch a game of chess. Suddenly, the boy refused to follow him regardless of life or death. He cried loudly and pulled his hand, insisting he go home. The old man loved his grandchild, so he complied with his wishes. After walking about 300 meters away from the entertainment area, he asked his grandchild why he was crying. The boy looked scared and shouted loudly:}
{align:justify|- Please run quickly, the people there have no heads, their whole bodies are covered in blood... Even if you do it, you're scared to death. What's the fun in going there? Don't you see?}
{align:justify|The two men were still chatting when from the air, a Japanese plane flew in, circled around and bombed the "Thang Ky Lau" building.}
{align:justify|Instantly everyone inside died, only a dozen people near the building escaped. The old man exclaimed: Unexpectedly, my nephew saved my life!}
{align:justify|This news was published in the Southeast Daily newspaper at the time, and all of Nanjing knew it.}
{align:justify|This proves: Children's souls are pure and pure, their vision can foresee strange things that are about to happen.}
{align:justify|Anhui province, Tuyen Chau town, Ton Phu town, recorded by old man Dinh Tiet.}
{align:justify|WIDE WIDOW}
{align:justify|Before liberation, in the town where my grandmother lived, there was an aunt named Vuong. Her husband passed away early, leaving only the orphans and widows to live together, experiencing many hardships and hardships, and the surrounding residents often helped them.}
{align:justify|After liberation, the widow of Vuong's family was classified as poor, with a good background, her son was accepted to work for the government, his status rose... Then he got married, she had a daughter-in-law, and their lives changed for the better.}
{align:justify|The poor wife now has a noble status, is the mother of a son with a high position, but she belongs to the class of petty people who, once in a position of advantage, become overbearing, treating people as nothing, she lives in the "inhumane servant" style, bluntly turning her back on the neighbors who used to wholeheartedly help her and her mother, in her eyes now there are only cadres and the commune, towards the neighbors around her she is cheap and contemptuous, seeing everyone as disgusting. eyes.}
{align:justify|Because she did not know how to create good deeds, her son soon died, and her daughter-in-law also quickly changed her marriage, because they and their husband had no children before... leaving her alone, living her miserable days.}
{align:justify|When she was over 70, she fell ill and was bedridden. Mr. A was a neighbor and gave her food. She no longer had the arrogant attitude she had before, but instead became polite and humble.}
{align:justify|She died, there wasn't even a coffin, so neighbors used mats to cover her, burying her body in the ground. It seemed like her last days of life ended in tragedy and coldness.}
{align:justify|But it's true that she wasn't so poor that she didn't have a coffin to bury, the person who created this tragedy was her trusted neighbor. It was Mr. A who created the tragedy of "death without a burial" for her.}
{align:justify|Originally, Mrs. Vuong trusted Mr. A very much, so before her death, she deposited the 300 VND of wealth she had accumulated and gave it to Mr. A to buy a coffin and take care of the funeral for her.}
{align:justify|But at that time, 300 VND was a huge amount of money, making Mr. A blinded by his greed, he silently swallowed that large amount of money. What Mr. A did was beyond his conscience.}
{align:justify|As a result, Mr. A did not enjoy long-term happiness, his family suddenly collapsed. He had two sons, but one was hit by a train and broke his leg, leaving him disabled for life, and the other died young. Neighbors all around said: Mr. A received retribution!}
{align:justify|Justify: Although Vuong's widow was arrogant and domineering, it was not the reason for her son's untimely fate. But people who are rich but do not cultivate kindness, do not pay attention to accumulating goodness to create blessings, live ungrateful lives... It's difficult to enjoy long-term happiness, and it's also impossible to find someone who lives honestly with you.}
{align:justify|As for Mr. A, he even dared to take and swallow the money to buy a coffin for the dead. Even if Ms. Vuong's soul was not haunted, it would be difficult for the heavens to tolerate. Because Mr. A dared to do this bad thing, he reaped the bad consequences, causing his family to fail.}
{align:justify|MY FATHER'S STORY}
{align:justify|My father said: At a time when the country was on fire, he was a student. At that time, there were two parties opposing each other. Party A bombed the school, causing many casualties.}
{align:justify|But the night before the disaster, my father happened to see a bat drowning in the pond. Feeling sorry for him, he immediately went to find a pole and let it down for the bat to cling to and swing up to save its life.}
{align:justify|The next morning, the disaster broke out, my father witnessed with his own eyes the students around him being bombed: The dead class, the injured class... One of his classmates had his head broken open, his brains flying everywhere right before his eyes.}
{align:justify|My father was fortunate to be safe and sound, of course he could have escaped on his own, but seeing that his classmates were injured, he could not bear to leave them alone, so he voluntarily stayed behind, loudly calling for everyone to join forces for rescue, so in the end he was captured by the terrorist party. They locked him up for nearly a week without food or water. On the sixth day, he took advantage of the guard's negligence and jumped from the third floor to an electric pole nearly two meters away, falling to the ground and escaping.}
{align:justify|My father told this story with the same indifference and calmness that people would tell. But it's hard for me to imagine the scene: A person locked up for six days without food or water can still use his determination and strength to jump from a building! If my father jumped and missed the pole, or if he was unlucky enough to get electrocuted, I wouldn't be sitting here writing this story right now.}
{align:justify|My father always reminds: "There is a god three meters above your head", so in life you must know how to do good and accumulate blessings. The mind always contains good thoughts. Don't criticize a small good but don't do it, don't criticize a small evil and do it forcefully.}
{align:justify|The words my father taught me, I always keep in my heart. I am very proud of my father's heart and way of life.}
{align:justify|Justify: From saving the drowning bat in the pond, to the determination not to run away, to stay in dangerous places to save classmates, it is enough for us to see the compassionate heart of our father in the story. A person with such spirituality, could his path fall into a dead end?}
{align:justify|STORIES OF DISCUSSES}
{align:justify|Ten years ago, my hometown had many bars and dance halls that on the outside were places to dance, but in reality they were hanging goats' heads to sell dog meat, because inside there were underground establishments selling many narcotics and providing sexual services, specializing in soliciting and setting traps to lure customers into indulgences. These dance halls are doing very well, and thanks to that, the directors are extremely rich and prosperous. Ten years have passed, looking back now, these entertainment venues have long been deserted and cold, all in decline.}
{align:justify|Director Khang, the owner of discotheque}
{align:justify|Mr. Khang also has terminal cancer, his family has long been broken up, and now lives in loneliness and loneliness. He has two children: A boy and a girl, but the boy joined a gang of gangsters and did bad things, so he was arrested and locked up by the government several times, and is still in prison. Girls are addicted to gambling, addicted to drugs, and prostitutes who sell their bodies for people's entertainment.}
{align:justify|Director B, now 50 years old, but his nightclub and sex establishment were both deleted, he had to go out to work as a construction contractor, but was defrauded by people of hundreds of thousands, so far he has not received any money.}
{align:justify|Finally, Y bar, famous for being a splendid and splendid place to entertain, it can be said that in the summer of 2005, the bar reached its peak, "rising like a kite in the wind"... However, suddenly a big fire broke out, causing this bar to burn down, causing a loss of more than two million. Currently, the director still owes a lot of money and has to run away.}
{align:justify|As for the female director surnamed Luu, when she was young, she and her husband opened a dance hall and prostitution establishment, earning over hundreds of thousands of black money. In our locality at that time, they contributed to the destruction of many families.}
{align:justify|Ms. Luu herself is very talented in business, so she quickly became rich. But "the happy scene did not last long", because her husband and a beautiful dancer held hands and ran away to build a love nest, leaving her alone to raise the child.}
{align:justify|Not long after, she fell into gambling and lost more and more money. In just seven years, the entire huge fortune was wiped out. Currently, she still owes high interest rates and is being forced and forced by gangsters to be very miserable.}
{align:justify|A quick look at the fate of bar and dance hall directors... It's clear that they live by relying on adultery and bullying to make their fortune. At first it seemed like they had made a big profit and were extremely rich, but in reality they later suffered terrible losses.}
{align:justify|It must be understood as: Even in their present life, they are rich and have many assets because they have accumulated deep blessings and virtues in the past. Therefore, in the present life you absolutely should not initiate karma through evil means, but should do business properly (right karma), then it is called knowing how to do business and make real money.}
{align:justify|If you get rich through illegal means, you certainly won't be able to keep the money for long, not to mention you will also bring deep evil karma into your body. You must know that money that is "imported" will certainly be "exported". If the money you receive is not clean, it will not be comfortable when you leave. Moreover, the hardships we witnessed them endure were just a warning... The real retribution has not yet begun.}
{align:justify|TRAN DAI GIA}
{align:justify|Mr. Tran is a smart and talented person. Handsome appearance, son of a wealthy family, generous personality, very charming and attractive speech.}
{align:justify|When he worked, people could only sell one or two products a month, but he could sell up to seven or eight sets of products every day. He is very talented at sales and is a genius in the business world.}
{align:justify|But he has a bad habit, which is that he loves to talk about clouds, rain, and wind, often looking for prostitutes to entertain him... He said he had orgies with many girls.}
{align:justify|I am a fellow karma, often trying to preach Buddha's teachings to dissuade you.}
{align:justify|I said: People with happiness and fortune... If you spend too much time with girls, you will lose your happiness, and people with thin blessings will have a shortened life span. Thanks to working together, he also listened to my advice to be restrained when dealing with women.}
{align:justify|Later, he moved to another place, opened a shop with his friends, and hung out with people full of beauty and entertainment, so he soon immersed himself in depravity and debauchery.}
{align:justify|He also boasted: Friends always advise girls to ruin their lives to increase their luck. That's why girls as young as 12 and 13 years old were abused by him and his friends who were deeply infected with this cruel and dishonest theory.}
{align:justify|I was very sad after hearing this, so I quickly advised him to stop and explained: This behavior is not a way of letting go of bad luck to help you become rich or increase your luck, but it only further destroys your happiness, fortune, and power and causes you to have a short life. Absolutely do not believe in this evil theory!}
{align:justify|But he still fanatically refused to listen, eager to spend money to destroy the lives of young women.}
{align:justify|About two or three months later, he was driving an open-top car on a trip with his partner when he was suddenly hit by a car, causing him to fly up to a height of more than ten meters and then fall down, his brain crushed, and his death horrifyingly tragic.}
{align:justify|Phung Tay Ngo}
{align:justify|MY CHILD}
{align:justify|I remember someone once asked His Holiness the Lama: Currently, China has fifteen million women having abortions every year. What message would you give to these people?}
{align:justify|Lama said:}
{align:justify|- Don't get pregnant. Use all methods to avoid getting pregnant. If you are pregnant, you should not have an abortion. Because the life you are carrying is most likely someone you love very much, or someone who loves you very much! We cannot know in advance, because right now we only care, only think about the responsibility to take care of the baby without knowing that it can change our whole life.}
{align:justify|I myself almost had an abortion and lost my child, but now the child is 5 years old. For all of this, I deeply understand it, engrave it in my bones.}
{align:justify|When I first got pregnant, I didn't know it. I just felt very tired and craved sleep. I could sleep up to 18 hours a day. Compared to a normal person who sleeps 6 hours a day, my drastic change made my husband panic. So he took me to the hospital to be examined. Go to the Institute of Chinese Medicine of Dong Thien Hospital, in Kuala Lumpur (Cua-la-Lampo).}
{align:justify|This hospital is an extremely famous private hospital in the Malaysian capital, with three institutes: Chinese Medicine, Western Medicine and Academia.}
{align:justify|Every year, the Institute of Chinese Medicine has Chinese scholars come for examination and exchange. At that time, the Chinese medicine hospital had the largest gathering of doctors. A Nanjing doctor checked my pulse and found no sign of pregnancy, so he gave me ten doses of medicine. I used two ladders when that night I suddenly had a dream: I saw a golden lotus flower falling from the sky, shining brightly. I woke up feeling very strange, so I went to buy a pregnancy test. Oh my God, two lines clearly appear, so I'm pregnant, what should I do?}
{align:justify|Because I didn't know I was pregnant, my husband and I flew for 4 hours. Everyone knows that air pressure is very detrimental to the fetus. Not only that, I also went to parties and drank a lot of wine, not to mention taking the vaccine. So I thought if I keep the baby, I'm afraid it won't be healthy, so get rid of it? It was so cruel, I fell into a dilemma. Finally, I decided to go with my husband to the Western Medicine Institute of Dong Thien Hospital to ask the doctor. Because Dong Thien is a very famous hospital: Doctors who work here must be highly skilled and have good techniques. Most of them study abroad from the UK or Canada. We chose Dr. Du Vi Van, he is about 50 years old, has studied abroad and has excellent karma in Canada, very talented and experienced.}
{align:justify|We told the doctor our situation, at that time I was inclined to eliminate the fetus. Doctor Du listened, pondered for a moment, then said:}
{align:justify|- I don't dare say that this baby will be healthy, but I believe that his vitality is very strong. If you two don't want to save the baby, then please look elsewhere, because I have never done abortion! If you choose to stay, then come see me tomorrow.}
{align:justify|My husband and I discussed for a day and finally decided: I had to grit my teeth and save the baby.}
{align:justify|The baby was three months old when I went to the hospital for a checkup. Seeing on the screen the baby moves non-stop. Doctor Du smiled and said: Well, it's a very agile and flexible baby, so that's good, it looks like the fetus is healthy.}
{align:justify|He then pointed to points on the screen explaining that these were the spine, arms, legs, etc.}
{align:justify|In the blink of an eye I felt the joy of being a mother, perhaps because I knew the fetus was healthy, and also because I was good at English, so after the examination that day, I chatted excitedly with the doctor and discovered: This doctor is not ordinary.}
{align:justify|Doctor Du is a second-generation descendant of Chinese people. After graduating from karma university in Canada, he returned home and worked at this hospital for more than twenty years. The doctor speaks English and Ma very fluently. He is also a very sincere Tantric practitioner.}
{align:justify|He said that in 2004, Thailand was hit by a great tsunami. At that time, this place needed a group of doctors to urgently help. Because citizens of Malaysia and Thailand could freely travel back and forth, Dr. Du immediately drove his family car straight to Phuket Island (Phuket). Whether it was treating victims or carrying corpses, he devoted all his strength to help. He did rescue work here for nearly five days, and after returning, he did not tell anyone about this gesture.}
{align:justify|The other day he came to visit the Master, a high monk Lama (he did not tell me his name). As soon as the master saw him, he said:}
{align:justify|- What did you do just now that there were so many people following behind? They are all foreigners.}
{align:justify|Hearing that, he looked at Master bewilderedly, because he saw that there were only two teachers and students in the room.}
{align:justify|Master smiled and continued:}
{align:justify|- I said, referring to the group of people following you.}
{align:justify|He was stunned in surprise. Suddenly I remembered that during five days on Pho-Ket Island, he helped handle nearly 200 bodies, and moreover, the victims were all Western tourists.}
{align:justify|The master smiled and said:}
{align:justify|- These people have completely good intentions towards you, so there is nothing to worry about.}
{align:justify|After the doctor told me, he said that after that he started to believe: There is a god three meters above his head, he must cherish all lives, that is why he is determined not to practice abortion.}
{align:justify|As time passes, the feelings in the mother's heart gradually grow. I was still worried about my baby so I went to "Thien Hau Cung" to get a tattoo.}
{align:justify|"Thien Hau Cung" was originally called "Hainan Hoi Quan", built by Chinese descendants who contributed money, considering each brick, blade of grass... None of this uses a penny from the government. Because it was founded by Hainan people, the Holy Mother Goddess is worshiped here. It is said that the tattoos here are extremely unique, so much so that later the name "Hai Nam Hoi Quan" was forgotten by people, on the contrary the name "Thien Hau Cung" became more and more famous.}
{align:justify|When I pulled out the card, I silently prayed what I wanted to ask, the result on the card was written in English like this: "You are pregnant, Please guardian Angel!..."}
{align:justify|The meaning is: You are pregnant, please invoke your guardian angel.}
{align:justify|I was a little surprised, thinking: "Probably just a coincidence".}
{align:justify|So I drew another card and got the same answer as last time.}
{align:justify|I feel like invisibly, heaven wants to treat this baby, I need to take care of him right now.}
{align:justify|In the blink of an eye, the fetus is nine months old. Because I fed it too much, it led to high blood pressure, so I had to go for many checkups.}
{align:justify|At the final diagnosis, I suddenly met a large group of doctors and medical students from the academy to consult. Here there is an Indian female doctor named Amy, who is a Lecturer at the academy. At this time, the screen clearly showed the baby's face, we could see it clearly. The Indian female doctor smiled and said:}
{align:justify|- "A boy! (A boy), I also saw it myself, but I still asked several times to make sure: "A boy? Are you sure?"}
{align:justify|- It's a boy, are you sure?}
{align:justify|- I assure you that it is true.}
{align:justify|Everyone confirms that. Doctor Du took a super B scan for me and recorded the documents. Because I was pregnant, my high blood pressure increased, so in the end it was decided to have a cesarean section, and the surgery will be at 9:30 a.m. on December 6.}
{align:justify|But the day before surgery, I had a very strange dream.}
{align:justify|My grandmother lived a very kind life when she was born. She passed away twenty years ago. I never dreamed of her until now. But that night I dreamed that I went to the Ancestor Church, my grandfather was lying on the bench, and I stood next to him with my belly hanging out, but he didn't seem to see me. She was dressed extremely beautiful and pure, her head was wearing a crown with a green gem, two holes in each ear, two earrings, also green gems. Even though I was dreaming, I remember this clearly: In ancient China, not everyone could arbitrarily pierce many ears and wear many earrings. Only people with noble status had the right to have many holes pierced and wear many earrings.}
{align:justify|After she passed away, my mother asked someone to tell me where she was born, and the answer was: My grandmother, thanks to her whole life of kindness and good heart, was able to go to a higher realm to practice. Now that I see her dressed so reverently, it seems that people are not wrong. The thing is, she doesn't seem to see me.}
{align:justify|At this time my grandfather pointed at her with a stick and asked:}
{align:justify|- What are you doing here?}
{align:justify|She replied, emphasizing twice:}
{align:justify|- I want to go back, I want to go back!}
{align:justify|After she answered, I suddenly woke up, sweat pouring down my body. Looking at the clock, it was exactly 5:30. Because I couldn't sleep anymore, I immediately prepared my luggage and went to the hospital. Previously, it was scheduled for 9:30 a.m. to give me a cesarean section. But right now it appeared that she was determined to stop and make things difficult, so the doctor was forced to negotiate with me.}
{align:justify|I say:}
{align:justify|- Okay, it's okay if I wait a bit.}
{align:justify|Unexpectedly, my daughter was born at nearly 12 o'clock.}
{align:justify|When the baby was born, my husband kept questioning the doctor:}
{align:justify|- Why did you say it was a boy before?}
{align:justify|Doctor Du fell into a difficult situation to explain, so he had to apologize, admitting that he had made a mistake. At that time I also believed: Wrong examination!}
{align:justify|But then thinking back, I found it absolutely impossible that it was a mistake! Doctor Du himself has decades of experience. I won't say anything for now, but at that time there were many witnesses at the scene, everyone acknowledged and affirmed the same thing, including the female Doctor Amy who had been teaching Obstetrics and Gynecology for more than ten years and the qualified doctors studying here! One viewer can be wrong, but it would be unreasonable for the whole group to be wrong. Even if the examination was wrong, the "chili" of the baby in the picture is still clearly visible, where did it come from?}
{align:justify|Therefore, it is impossible for a doctor to admit that he or she made a mistake. Absolutely not a wrong examination! The most thrilling thing is that my daughter's earlobes have blurred outlines, as if she had had two holes pierced and was wearing cotton. Could it be that the baby about to be born is a boy, but when my grandmother decides to return, the fetus turns out to be a girl? These are just silent doubts in my heart.}
{align:justify|When the baby was full month old, I went to "Thien Hau Cung" to get a tattoo card to see what the baby's fate was? Because the baby was only 2 and a half kilograms when he was born, he was in a critical condition, and because I had to take medicine for high blood pressure, I was a little worried about the baby. As a result, the card reads: "Red light shines on the head, noble people come to the house". It was almost 12 noon when my child was born, which is true: Red light shines above your head!}
{align:justify|When I was almost a year old, my marriage had conflicts, leading to no way to maintain it. As a result, I took my child and returned home. At that time, I was very afraid that my mother would not accept me, because she is the type of person who values face too much and has a tendency to favor men over women.}
{align:justify|Who would have thought that my mother loved me so much. In fact, when my grandmother was still alive, my mother and she had a very good relationship, so much so that when she passed away, many years later my mother still missed her. One time my mother scolded her grandchild: Hey! I don't know why she has this... Are puppies like you captivating?}
{align:justify|During this time, because my husband and I were constantly arguing, I didn't care about the future. That night I was on duty at the power plant. While talking on the phone with my husband, I felt very angry and upset. I immediately turned off the phone, turned on the generator and suddenly felt the desire to commit suicide. This is a high-voltage karma zone, if I just put my hand in, I can end my life, end all the suffering, and there's no one around right now, if something happens, everyone will think it was an unexpected accident. So my daughter can enjoy an allowance, and I also get liberation.}
{align:justify|I was thinking like that, when suddenly I felt crazy in my stomach, constantly thinking about my child, so I couldn't act rashly, my insides struggled for two hours. In the end, it seemed like there was a very strong invisible force stopping me. I thought about my child's misfortune of not being loved by his father. If I died, his life would be as fragile as a blade of grass. So I wiped my tears, held onto the wall, and staggered out like a soulless corpse.}
{align:justify|The next day, my mother suddenly worriedly asked me:}
{align:justify|- Did nothing happen last night?}
{align:justify|I was startled, thinking she had seen right through my heart, so I quickly said it over:}
{align:justify|- No, it's nothing, mom.}
{align:justify|Hearing that, my mother breathed a sigh of relief and said:}
{align:justify|- Nothing is fine. Because last night she kept crying and calling for mommy, mommy, making me think something happened to her?}
{align:justify|I hastily asked: What time was it?}
{align:justify|- Around 6 o'clock to 8 o'clock! He kept crying and calling for his mother continuously! No matter how much you coax me, I won't be able to calm down. It makes me tired to death.}
{align:justify|From 6 o'clock to 8 o'clock was the time when I was in the power plant and wanted to commit suicide. It's true that I was called back by her, because she is a particularly happy and easy-to-raise child. Almost never sick, but also doesn't bother people. Moreover, the situation of him screaming and crying like that only happened once, it never happened before, and it won't happen again. At that time, I took the risk to save the fetus, who would have thought that one day the baby would save my life.}
{align:justify|My child does not show any signs of outstanding intelligence. Except for his interest in fine arts (which is the basic genetic gene of his parents), he has nothing outstanding worth mentioning. It also does not inherit any advantages or strengths of its parents. But I always think: Why do we ordinary people rely on intelligence and beauty to judge a person's fortunes and misfortunes? Because how many children, at first seem smart and clever, but later cause their parents many troubles and troubles? There have been so many beautiful little girls, but after growing up, they could not escape the life of "red beauty".}
{align:justify|Currently, there are many young women around me who are worrying about taking drugs or drinking a lot of alcohol because they don't want to keep their children. They make their bodies less healthy and are not good for the fetus, then use the excuse of fearing that the child will not be smart enough or have an abnormal physical condition... If they have enough reason to easily abort the fetus, just like I almost aborted my child in the past. There is nothing to say about abortion surgery being dangerous because any surgery is dangerous. The important thing is that when you kill your child, you don't know that the child you aborted was the most loved person in your life, or the person who brought you the most luck?}
{align:justify|I remember when my daughter was almost three years old, my mother wanted me to remarry, I didn't agree, so we argued. This went by for about a few months. One day, my daughter was playing with her when she suddenly said: Grandma, please don't force my mother anymore, it makes me very sad.}
{align:justify|My mother heard him say and could only shed tears, then she told me:}
{align:justify|- If you have a child like that, I really don't have to worry.}
{align:justify|After taking refuge in the Three Jewels, I took my children to Pho Da Son, where there is the famous Mai Phuc meditation institute. Everyone knows that there are several nuns here who practice very deeply. That day, when I brought my child up to the place, I met an old nun basking in the sun. When she saw my child, she immediately called us over and said many very auspicious things.}
{align:justify|As for the Master I took refuge in, he was a Bhikkhunī who was about twenty years old. Master left the home life as a child and graduated from Karma Buddha Academy in Minnan (Fujian). During the process of being with Master, I realized that she had supernatural powers, but Master never claimed to have extraordinary powers. But whatever I think, the Master knows everything. The monk always told me to take good care of the baby. Sometimes I couldn't help but complain to the Master that she was so stupid. The monk just smiled without saying anything, then humorously said: If you don't want to raise the baby then let me!}
{align:justify|My mother often sneaks out to see my future. Coincidentally, many famous fortune tellers say: My child brings fortune! It's strange to say that when I returned home with my child for a while, it was easy to apply for a job at a karma university. Moreover, before I came to work, this agency was not very generous. But since I started working, my efficiency suddenly increased. Thanks to that, in addition to my monthly salary, I regularly receive bonuses, enjoy preferential treatment, and have the right to buy necessities at special prices. Even though I became a single mother raising my children alone, my finances were relatively good. Many prophets, including my master, have said that my future will be extremely good. Actually I think: If worldly people say good old age, they must first base it on good children, because: "I'm not afraid that my career won't be successful, I'm just afraid that my children won't be good"... This is the important thing that makes it difficult for us to be happy.}
{align:justify|I bring my own experiences and share them with everyone, hoping that all, especially young women, will behave well with the seeds of life that have just been imaged in their hearts. Western European countries often criticize our country on human rights issues, and at first I thought it was a political conspiracy. But now I no longer see it like that, because when I travel around countries like: Singapore, Thailand, India, Malaysia etc… I don't see any other country like ours, a country where right from the press to every corner, literally everywhere, it promotes, encourages, and glorifies abortion! Even boasted that: Abortion is painless! How can it not be painful? Not to mention that reincarnated child, who has a very deep relationship with me, is blood in blood, flesh in flesh... with me. Yet we have no choice but to destroy them. By doing so, we are also destroying the happiness of our lives!}
{align:justify|I hope that men who read this article should be responsible towards their families when they are pregnant with their children. If you live irresponsibly, you will not harm one life, but harm two lives. According to the rotating law of cause and effect, what you create will eventually be returned to you. Please don't think it's because you're pregnant, even if you abort it, it'll just be a small spot of blood. In fact, when the embryo already has consciousness, the baby still knows pain, sadness, anger, and hatred, and knows fear when hearing the parents abort it. It's just that it can't speak or express it for the parents to understand. When the fetus is too large and is aborted, the baby's head, arms, and legs are cut off to be pulled out... heartbreakingly painful. Taking life is equivalent to murder. What's more, it was a child. Which parent could bear to watch their child being painfully mutilated? If the baby was just a ball of blood, that ball of blood would still feel pain and suffering when forced to die... Therefore, please never have an abortion.}
{align:justify|Tho Dang Hy}
{align:justify|EXPERIENCE OF PRAYING FOR ABORTION}
{align:justify|In 2001, my daughter accidentally got pregnant a second time. She called to ask what to do? I said: Abortion is a serious crime, so if you are already pregnant, you must be born, absolutely do not abort!}
{align:justify|My daughter already has a 7-year-old son, so she really wants to have another girl. She feels that this pregnancy's reaction is different from the previous one, so she thinks it's very likely to be a girl, so she agrees to my opinion.}
{align:justify|Who would have thought that three months later, when the hospital examined them, they discovered that the fetus had no heartbeat and had stopped growing for a week. That's why the doctor suggested surgery to remove it, so my child agreed.}
{align:justify|After I studied Buddhism, it is very important to understand that the dead still have a bardo body for 49 days, so during this time, if the deceased's relatives chant Buddhist sutras and deliverance to them, it will be very effective and beneficial, because after 49 days they will rely on the support of their relatives to create goodness and be reborn in a good state.}
{align:justify|Therefore, after knowing that my daughter was forced to have an abortion, I decided to devote all my efforts to the unfortunate death of the little fetus, reciting the 7 sets of Ksitigarbha Sutras to pray for her rebirth.}
{align:justify|I think this baby, when she was conceived, abused her mother for about three months before leaving. It seems clear that the unjust bondholders came to seek revenge, so my chanting sutras can help both sides resolve the injustice and also help my daughter be safe and sound.}
{align:justify|Because I was worried that my daughter wouldn't take good care of herself. If she didn't rest well, she could easily get sick, so from Nanjing I quickly bought a ticket to Beijing to take care of my daughter and chant sutras deliverance for her.}
{align:justify|Because bus tickets are difficult to buy and I need to go urgently, so I have to use black market tickets. I went to my daughter's house the next afternoon, after dinner I was exhausted, so I whispered to the fetus:}
{align:justify|Honey, I'm so tired today, so tomorrow morning, I'll start chanting sutras for you.}
{align:justify|But just after 4 a.m., my son-in-law came into the room and woke me up, saying:}
{align:justify|Mom, please go sleep with baby Tai, Ngoc Han (my daughter's name) had a severe stomachache all night long, now I have to take my wife to the hospital for a check-up.}
{align:justify|I looked at the clock and saw that it was almost 5 o'clock, so I quickly went to recite the Ksitigarbha Sutra, reciting the first set.}
{align:justify|My daughter went to the hospital for a check-up and found there was no problem, so she went back home to lie down and the pain was gone.}
{align:justify|Later my friends analyzed and interpreted that: Maybe because I made vows chanting sutras deliverance for the baby, he did it to warn me to chant it early.}
{align:justify|Because I had just gone through a long and tiring trip, every day I had to take care of cooking, taking care of my daughter and chanting sutras to pray for her, so I was very busy. At noon, when I rested a bit, I took advantage of chanting the Ksitigarbha sutras. After cooking dinner, do the evening meditation and recite Buddha's name for an hour.}
{align:justify|At this time I am 67 years old, although I feel very tired, I am always confident in my heart, because I think I am doing what a Buddha disciple needs to do.}
{align:justify|These days, whenever I finish chanting at night, I'm so tired that I immediately fall asleep as soon as I lie down, without any dreams.}
{align:justify|But one night, I saw a strange dream and after waking up I still remember it very clearly: I dreamed that I heard the sound of two people talking to each other next door, one said:}
{align:justify|- Observe to see where this death will be born? Heaven or human world?}
{align:justify|The other replied: As far as I can see, this death will be born in heaven!}
{align:justify|When I heard this, I suddenly woke up and was very surprised.}
{align:justify|I haven't had a dream in many nights, moreover, since studying Buddhism until now, I have never had a dream with such strange content.}
{align:justify|I suddenly remembered that in the Ksitigarbha Sutra it said: If the relatives and friends have finished chanting enough, the spirit will be liberated. So have I chanted the sutras seven times?}
{align:justify|Because I have been so busy these past few days that I have not paid attention to counting the number of sutras I have recited. Now I'm just starting to do the math: “On Wednesday afternoon I arrived in Beijing, on Thursday morning I started reciting, so last night was Wednesday, I just finished seven sets.”}
{align:justify|In my heart, I am very happy, not because since I studied Buddhism, this is the first time I have seen a dream with a special content, but because this dream gives me a clear understanding: I successfully chanted the sutras to pray for my grandchild, proving that the words of all Buddhas and Bodhisattva are not false. I understand more deeply the sentence: The words all Buddhas, Bodhisattva are true words, true words, not false... described in the Diamond Sutra.}
{align:justify|This dream I saw very clearly and had a deep impression, I silently thanked all Buddhas, Bodhisattva for giving me hints, making me have even more solid faith in studying Buddha.}
{align:justify|I immediately got up from my bed and went before all Buddhas and Bodhisattva to sincerely bow and recite a thousand names of Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva to express my endless gratitude.}
{align:justify|The next day I thought: "The delivery has been completed successfully, my daughter's health has also recovered well", so I allow myself to relax, have the right to enjoy a little leisure and entertainment, to compensate for the tiring days.}
{align:justify|Just that night, the television showed a detective movie that I really liked (because I hadn't studied Buddhism deeply enough so I couldn't resist the temptation of the movie).}
{align:justify|So that afternoon I worked hard to finish my classes early, so that I could have time to leisurely watch movies in the evening.}
{align:justify|Last night, while I was watching a movie alone in my room, I suddenly heard a noise outside the door. Please explain: My daughter's doorknob is horizontal, not circular. Every time I turn it, it changes from horizontal to vertical. I closely watched the doorknob rotate and change from horizontal to vertical very clearly, so I was convinced that baby Tai wanted to come in and play with me. But I waited for a long time and still didn't see him come in, so I thought to myself: “It's good that you don't come in and make too much noise, it looks like I can watch the movie in peace.”}
{align:justify|But just as the movie ended, I suddenly heard a voice calling from outside the door: Grandma!}
{align:justify|I silently complimented: This boy is so good, he waited until I finished watching the movie before asking to come in and play, so he spoke up:}
{align:justify|- Tai, come here with me!}
{align:justify|But there was no response, nor did I hear any movement outside.}
{align:justify|I immediately walked to the door and opened it, looked around and saw no one outside.}
{align:justify|I immediately called: Tai!}
{align:justify|My daughter was lying in the next room and quickly spoke up:}
{align:justify|- The kid has been downstairs to play for a long time, mom.}
{align:justify|I ask:}
{align:justify|- So didn't he come to open the door to his mother's room twenty minutes ago?}
{align:justify|He went down to play so it's been over an hour now, he's not here.}
{align:justify|So was it you or someone else who turned the doorknob in mom's room?}
{align:justify|Ngoc Han replied:}
{align:justify|We all want mom to watch movies in peace, no one is going to bother her!}
{align:justify|I say:}
{align:justify|- That's not true, someone actually came and turned the door handle to make it move, and mom still clearly heard the voice calling "ma'am"!}
{align:justify|At this time, I suddenly remembered that in the Hundred Karma Sutras there is a passage that says: Newly born gods have the principle that they will immediately do three things:}

{align:justify|I immediately understood: This is definitely the fetus that has already given birth and has come down to thank me, because if the child is born smoothly, he will also call me grandmother.}
{align:justify|I myself am inherently a rational person. Since studying Buddhism until now, I have not had any hallucinations. Moreover, these events occurred after I had chanted the sutras to pray for complete repose, and at a time when I was completely relaxed, they absolutely cannot be attributed to hallucinations or explained in similar ways.}
{align:justify|I suddenly remembered the dream from the previous day and my heart was secretly shocked. I was even more deeply absorbed in the words of all Buddhas and Bodhisattva, which were extremely true and not false, and I suddenly realized: The merits of the Ksitigarbha Sutra are immeasurably wonderful.}
{align:justify|When I first studied Buddhism, when reading the Ksitigarbha Sutra, I only thought that all Buddhas and Bodhisattva preached like that because they wanted to teach evil people to be good, so I did not completely believe in the words in the sutra. Even when reading the Hundred Karma Sutras, I still see how the stories told here are like myths.}
{align:justify|However, after experiencing this and other incidents, I have deeply felt that: Although the Buddha Sutras make people feel too mysterious, far-fetched, difficult to understand, hard to think about, what all Buddhas and Bodhisattva said is indeed very true, not false. As long as we have solid faith and practice honestly as the Buddha taught, we will experience the Buddha's inherent nature in each person.}
{align:justify|From then on, I felt deep gratitude towards Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva: No matter where I go, whenever I see His statue, I sincerely worship him. Because Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva helped me increase my faith in learning Buddha, thanks to the true merit of Bodhisattva and Ksitigarbha Sutra... guided and helped me steadfastly walk on Buddha's path of wisdom enlightenment.}
{align:justify|Today is Ksitigarbha Bodhisattva's birthday. To repay his endless gratitude, last night I wrote this essay. I would like to bring a part of my personal experience and respectfully share it with everyone. I hope you can deeply believe in cause and effect and deeply believe in Buddha's words: No killing, no abortion. Sincerely repentance all the karma created in the past. Please chant the sutras deliverance for the sake of the sentient beings you have harmed in the past, praying for them to be born in a good land to meet the Buddha's practice and attain Bodhi.}
{align:justify|Van Phong}
